window.UMMAHTI_GUIDE={"source":"Ummahti Quran app: feature/guide GuideCatalog.kt and GuideCitations.kt (reviewed entries only)","categories":["Worship & Prayer","The Qur’an","Heart & Emotions","Trials & Patience","Faith & Repentance","Family & Relationships","Work, Study & Rizq","Life & Decisions","Dreams & Signs","Daily Life & Dhikr"],"topics":[{"id":"maghrib_prayer_and_after","k":0,"t":"Maghrib: During Prayer or After?","s":"What do I read during Maghrib?","e":"This usually means one of two things. Inside the prayer itself you recite al-Fatihah and a short surah in the first two rak’ahs, as in any prayer. After the prayer, many keep to Ayat al-Kursi and the usual remembrance said after salah.","a":["If you meant after the prayer, the remembrance reported for after every prayer is in the topic linked below."],"q":[[2,255,255]],"h":[],"f":["remembrance_around_prayer","morning_and_evening_remembrance","focus_in_prayer"],"m":false,"w":["maghrib","what do i read during maghrib","maghrib prayer","after maghrib","مغرب","maghrib gebet","priere du maghrib","prière du maghrib","magrib","salat maghrib","sholat maghrib","магриб","aksam namazi","akşam namazı","مغرب کی نماز"],"d":[0],"l":"en"},{"id":"focus_in_prayer","k":0,"t":"Focus in Prayer","s":"Losing focus during salah","e":"Khushu‘ is not a switch you flip once; it is something every worshipper works at for a lifetime. Slow down, understand what you are saying, and each time your attention wanders, bring it back without scolding yourself.","a":["Slow every movement down and pause briefly between them, rather than rushing through.","Learn the meaning of what you recite in salah; understanding tends to hold attention."],"q":[[23,1,2],[20,14,14]],"h":[],"f":["protection_from_whispers","missing_salah"],"m":false,"w":["focus in prayer","khushu","khushoo","can't focus in salah","concentration in salah","cant focus in salah","losing focus praying","mind wanders in salah","i feel nothing when i pray","prayer feels empty","salah feels empty","no feeling in salah","خشوع"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"missing_salah","k":0,"t":"Missing Prayers","s":"Getting back to salah","e":"The Qur’an names people who neglected the prayer, and then immediately excepts those who turn back. The door is open. Do not try to repair years in one night. Start with the next prayer that is due.","a":["Pray the next prayer at its time today. One on time is the beginning, not the whole repair.","Ask a person of knowledge what is due for prayers you have missed, rather than guessing at it alone."],"q":[[19,59,60],[20,14,14],[29,45,45],[4,103,103]],"h":[0,1,2],"f":["laziness_and_discipline","weak_faith_returning_to_allah","focus_in_prayer"],"m":false,"w":["praying on time","pray on time","prayer on time","delaying prayer","delaying my prayer","i keep delaying my prayer","i pray late","praying late","الصلاة على وقتها","تأخير الصلاة","gebet rechtzeitig","prier a l heure","prier à l'heure","sholat tepat waktu","menunda sholat","намаз вовремя","откладываю намаз","namazi vaktinde kilmak","namazı vaktinde kılmak","namazi geciktirmek","namazı geciktirmek","نماز وقت پر","نماز میں تاخیر","missing salah","missed prayers","i don't pray","i dont pray","stopped praying","missing prayers","qada prayers","qadha prayers","qaza namaz","make up prayers","left salah","start praying again","getting back to prayer","ترك الصلاة","تارك الصلاة","gebete verpasst","bete nicht","priere manquee","prière manquée","je ne prie pas","meninggalkan sholat","tidak sholat","пропустил намаз","не молюсь","namaz kilmiyorum","namaz kılmıyorum","kaza namazi","kaza namazı","نماز چھوٹ","نماز نہیں پڑھتا"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"laziness_and_discipline","k":0,"t":"Laziness and Consistency","s":"No motivation to keep going","e":"Motivation is not the condition Allah placed on worship; steadiness is. The Prophet ﷺ sought refuge from laziness by name, which tells you it is an ordinary human weight and not a verdict on your faith. Choose something small you can keep.","a":["Pick one act small enough that you could still do it on your worst day, and hold to that.","When you slip, resume at the next opportunity instead of waiting for a fresh start."],"q":[[20,132,132],[70,22,23],[2,45,45]],"h":[1],"f":["missing_salah","weak_faith_returning_to_allah","breaking_a_harmful_habit"],"m":false,"w":["lazy","laziness","no motivation","can't be consistent","consistency","discipline","stay consistent","staying consistent","be consistent","procrastinating","procrastination","keep putting things off","لازم","كسل","الكسل","kasal","كسل","الكسل","التسويف","faulheit","keine motivation","paresse","manque de motivation","malas","tidak konsisten","лень","нет мотивации","tembellik","motivasyon yok","سستی","کاہلی"],"d":[1],"l":"en"},{"id":"asking_allah_dua","k":0,"t":"Asking Allah","s":"How to make du‘a","e":"There is no special formula and no gatekeeper. Allah says He is near and answers the one who calls. Speak in your own language, ask for what you actually need, and ask often. Asking is itself worship, not an interruption of it.","a":["Say it plainly, in your own language, in your own words. No fixed wording is required.","Keep asking. Repeating a du‘a is not nagging Allah; it is what reliance looks like."],"q":[[2,186,186],[40,60,60],[7,55,55]],"h":[3],"f":["delayed_dua","tawakkul_trust_in_allah","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["how to make dua","how do i make dua","how to pray to allah","asking allah","make dua","making dua","supplication","best way to make dua","dua","sleep dua","dua for\n                // travel","dua for exam","dua\n                // for healing","how to make dua","dua","دعاء","doa","bittgebet","invocation","دعاء\n                // السفر","دعاء المريض","دعاء الاستخارة","doa makan","doa perjalanan","كيف ادعو","كيف ادعو الله","كيفية الدعاء","wie macht man dua","wie mache ich dua","comment faire une invocation","comment invoquer allah","cara berdoa","cara berdoa yang benar","как делать дуа","мольба","dua nasil yapilir","dua nasıl yapılır","دعا کیسے مانگیں"],"d":[2,3,4],"l":"en"},{"id":"delayed_dua","k":0,"t":"When a Du‘a Feels Unanswered","s":"You have been asking for a long time","e":"Yunus ﷺ called out from inside the darkness, and the Qur’an says Allah responded and delivered him, but not on the timetable he would have chosen. Delay is not refusal. Keep asking, and do not let impatience become the thing that stops you.","a":["Keep making the same du‘a, and add asking Allah for what is best in the matter.","Take the practical steps that are in your hands while you wait; du‘a and effort belong together."],"q":[[2,186,186],[21,87,88],[12,86,86],[40,60,60]],"h":[4],"f":["asking_allah_dua","contentment_with_qadr","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["dua not answered","unanswered dua","my dua is not answered","allah is not answering","been making dua for years","dua rejected","why is my dua not accepted","waiting for my dua","لم يستجب دعائي","دعائي لم يستجب","dua nicht erhort","dua nicht erhört","invocation non exaucee","invocation non exaucée","doa tidak dikabulkan","doa belum terkabul","дуа не принята","молитва не отвечена","duam kabul olmuyor","duam kabul olmadi","duam kabul olmadı","دعا قبول نہیں"],"d":[3],"l":"en"},{"id":"night_prayer","k":0,"t":"Praying at Night","s":"Tahajjud and Qiyam al-Layl","e":"The night prayer is voluntary, and that is precisely its worth: nobody sees it. Begin with two units before Fajr on one night this week rather than a plan you will abandon by Thursday.","a":["Set your alarm twenty minutes before Fajr on one night, and pray two units.","Use that time to ask Allah for the thing you most need. Say it out loud if that helps."],"q":[[17,79,79],[51,17,18],[39,9,9]],"h":[],"f":["laziness_and_discipline","asking_allah_dua","before_sleeping"],"m":false,"w":["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam al layl","qiyam ul layl","praying at night","waking up to pray","last third of the night","تهجد","قيام الليل","nachtgebet","priere de nuit","prière de nuit","tahajud","sholat malam","ночная молитва","teheccud","gece namazi","gece namazı","تہجد"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"jumuah_friday","k":0,"t":"Jumu‘ah (Friday)","s":"What to read and do on Friday","e":"Friday carries its own gathered prayer and its own recommended practices: reciting Surah al-Kahf, and sending abundant salawat upon the Prophet ﷺ.","a":["Recite Surah al-Kahf sometime on Friday, and increase your salawat upon the Prophet ﷺ."],"q":[[62,9,10],[18,1,10]],"h":[5,6],"f":["focus_in_prayer","dunya_is_temporary"],"m":false,"w":["jumuah","jumma","juma","friday prayer","surah kahf friday","friday","جمعة"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"ramadan_fasting","k":0,"t":"Ramadan and Fasting","s":"Fasting in Ramadan","e":"Ramadan is the month the Qur’an was revealed, and fasting it is prescribed as a means to taqwa, an awareness of Allah, rather than as an end in itself.","a":["Pair your fast with extra Qur’an and du‘a; the reward is tied to sincerity, not endurance alone.","In the last ten nights, give part of each night to prayer and du‘a, and seek Laylat al-Qadr especially in the odd nights.","For who is excused from fasting, or how to make up a fast you missed, ask a person of knowledge."],"q":[[2,183,185],[2,186,186],[97,1,5]],"h":[7,8,9],"f":["night_prayer","reading_the_quran_daily","asking_a_person_of_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["ramadan","ramadhan","ramazan","fasting","sawm","roza","rozah","laylatul qadr","laylat al qadr","laylat ul qadr","lailatul qadr","night of qadr","night of power","night of decree","last ten nights","iftar","iftar dua","dua for iftar time","dua when breaking fast","suhoor","suhur","sehri","sahur","رمضان","صيام","ليلة القدر","العشر الاواخر","الافطار","السحور","fastenmonat","nacht der bestimmung","fastenbrechen","nuit du destin","rupture du jeune","rupture du jeûne","jeune","jeûne","puasa","puasa ramadhan","lailatul qadar","doa berbuka","doa berbuka puasa","рамадан","пост","ночь предопределения","ифтар","сухур","oruc","oruç","kadir gecesi","iftar duasi","iftar duası","روزہ","شب قدر","افطار کی دعا","سحری"],"d":[5,6],"l":"en"},{"id":"dua_in_sujood","k":0,"t":"Asking While in Sujood","s":"Supplicating in prostration","e":"Prostration is the position the Sunnah names as the nearest a servant comes to their Lord, and the instruction that follows straight after it is to ask, and to ask a lot. There is no list you have to complete and no language you are required to use. Ask in the words you actually have, for the thing you actually need. Nearness is what is reported here; a particular outcome is not.","a":["After the remembrance you already say in prostration, ask for one thing you genuinely need, in your own language.","If nothing comes to mind, ask for what you would ask for if you knew this were your last prayer."],"q":[[96,19,19],[7,55,55],[2,186,186]],"h":[10],"f":["asking_allah_dua","focus_in_prayer","delayed_dua"],"m":false,"w":["Sajdah","sujood","sajdah","sajda","sujood","sujud","prostration","dua in sujood","dua in sujud","supplication in prostration","what to say in sujood","what do i say in sujood","closest to allah in sujood","nearest to allah in prostration","asking in sajdah","dua in sajdah","praying in prostration","الدعاء في السجود","أقرب ما يكون العبد","bittgebet in der niederwerfung","dua in der sujud","invocation en prosternation","priere en prosternation","doa dalam sujud","berdoa saat sujud","дуа в сажда","молитва в поклоне","secdede dua","sucudda dua","سجدے میں دعا","سجدے کی دعا"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"prostration_of_forgetfulness","k":0,"t":"A Mistake in Your Prayer","s":"Forgetting during prayer (sujud as-sahw)","e":"The most useful true thing to know here is that the Prophet ﷺ forgot in prayer. He ended one prayer two units short, was told so, and completed it and made two prostrations. He did not abandon it and start again. Your prayer is very rarely ruined by a mistake. Which errors call for those two prostrations, and whether they come before or after the closing salutation, is answered differently by different schools of law, so take that detail to someone qualified rather than to guesswork.","a":["Do not restart the prayer in a panic. Complete it, then make the two prostrations.","Ask a person of knowledge, once and calmly, which mistakes require this in the school you follow."],"q":[[2,286,286]],"h":[11],"f":["asking_a_person_of_knowledge","focus_in_prayer","missing_salah"],"m":false,"w":["sajdah","sajda","sujood","sujud","prostration","sujud al sahw","sujood al sahw","sajdah sahw","sajda sahw","prostration of forgetfulness","forgetfulness in prayer","i made a mistake in my prayer","made a mistake in salah","forgot a rakat","forgot a rakah","lost count in salah","did i pray three or four","mistake in salah","سجود السهو","سهو في الصلاة","vergessen im gebet","fehler im gebet","oubli dans la priere","erreur dans la priere","sujud sahwi","lupa rakaat","salah rakaat","ошибка в намазе","забыл ракат","sehiv secdesi","namazda hata","rekat sasirdim","سجدہ سہو","نماز میں غلطی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"waking_for_fajr","k":0,"t":"Waking for Fajr","s":"Sleeping through the dawn prayer","e":"Missing fajr again and again wears a person down more than most missed prayers, because it happens while you are asleep and so feels like something you cannot help. What is reported about it is practical rather than condemning: a sleeper is held by three knots, and they come undone one at a time: by remembering Allah, then by ablution, then by prayer. And if you did sleep through it, the instruction is to pray it when you wake, not to carry it around all day.","a":["Move the decision to the night before: sleep earlier, and put the alarm out of arm’s reach.","If you wake and the time has passed, pray it then. Do not add a day of guilt on top of a missed prayer."],"q":[[17,78,78],[11,114,114],[20,130,130]],"h":[12,0],"f":["missing_salah","laziness_and_discipline","night_prayer"],"m":false,"w":["dua when waking up","dua for waking up","waking up dua","dua after waking","fajr","fajar","waking up for fajr","wake up for fajr","cant wake up for fajr","cannot wake up for fajr","sleeping through fajr","slept through fajr","missed fajr","i always miss fajr","waking up early to pray","subh prayer","fajr prayer","morning prayer","الفجر","صلاة الفجر","الاستيقاظ للفجر","fajr gebet","morgengebet","zum fajr aufwachen","priere du fajr","priere de l aube","se lever pour le fajr","sholat subuh","bangun subuh","kesiangan subuh","фаджр","утренняя молитва","проспал фаджр","sabah namazi","sabah namazı","imsak","sabaha kalkmak","فجر","فجر کی نماز","فجر کے لیے اٹھنا"],"d":[7,8],"l":"en"},{"id":"remembrance_around_prayer","k":0,"t":"Remembrance Around the Prayer","s":"After the call, and after salah","e":"Each prayer is framed by a few words of remembrance. When the call to prayer is heard, the Sunnah gives a supplication asking Allah to raise the Prophet ﷺ to the station He promised him. When the prayer ends, the Prophet ﷺ asked Allah’s forgiveness three times and praised Him, and he taught glorifying, praising and magnifying Allah after every prayer. None of it takes more than a few minutes.","a":["After your next prayer, stay seated for a few minutes and say these before you get up.","When you hear the adhan, listen to it through, then say the supplication taught for after the call."],"q":[[4,103,103],[2,152,152]],"h":[13,14],"f":["focus_in_prayer","missing_salah","morning_and_evening_remembrance"],"m":false,"w":["dua after salah","dua after prayer","dua after namaz","after salah","after prayer","what to say after prayer","what to say after salah","what to read after salah","adhkar after salah","adhkar after prayer","dhikr after prayer","dhikr after salah","tasbih after prayer","tasbih after salah","33 times after prayer","allahumma antas salam","adhan","azan","athan","call to prayer","dua after adhan","dua after azan","what to say after the adhan","when i hear the adhan","اذكار بعد الصلاة","دعاء بعد الصلاة","دعاء بعد الاذان","الاذان","dua nach dem gebet","gebetsruf","dua nach dem adhan","invocations apres la priere","invocations après la prière","appel a la priere","appel à la prière","dzikir setelah sholat","doa setelah sholat","wirid setelah sholat","doa setelah adzan","adzan","азкары после намаза","дуа после намаза","дуа после азана","азан","namaz sonrasi tesbihat","namaz sonrası tesbihat","ezan duasi","ezan duası","ezan","نماز کے بعد کے اذکار","نماز کے بعد کی دعا","اذان کے بعد کی دعا","اذان"],"d":[9,10],"l":"en"},{"id":"wudu_and_purity","k":0,"t":"Wudu and Purity","s":"Preparing for prayer","e":"The Qur’an itself names the washing that comes before prayer, and in the same verse says that Allah does not intend to make things hard for you, but to purify you. The Prophet ﷺ called purification half of faith. The detailed rulings, such as what breaks wudu and when ghusl or tayammum is needed, are where the schools of law differ in their details, so learn them from someone qualified rather than from an app.","a":["Make your next wudu slowly and with attention, as preparation for standing before Allah rather than a task to get through.","For what breaks wudu, and for ghusl or tayammum, ask a person of knowledge rather than guessing."],"q":[[5,6,6],[9,108,108]],"h":[15,16],"f":["asking_a_person_of_knowledge","focus_in_prayer","missing_salah"],"m":false,"w":["wudu","wudhu","wuzu","ablution","ablutions","taharah","tahara","purification","how to make wudu","how to do wudu","making wudu","dua after wudu","after wudu","what to say after wudu","virtue of wudu","الوضوء","وضوء","الطهارة","دعاء بعد الوضوء","فضل الوضوء","rituelle waschung","gebetswaschung","les ablutions","faire ses ablutions","berwudhu","doa setelah wudhu","bersuci","омовение","тахарат","вуду","abdest","abdest almak","abdest duasi","abdest duası","وضو","وضو کی دعا","وضو کا طریقہ"],"d":[11],"l":"en"},{"id":"reading_the_quran_daily","k":1,"t":"Reading the Qur’an Every Day","s":"Starting, and staying with it","e":"Most people who feel far from the Qur’an are not lazy. They set out to read a great deal, missed a day, felt they had broken something, and stopped altogether. The Qur’an itself was not sent down all at once; it came in stages, to be read over a long time. A small amount you keep for months is worth more than a page you dread.","a":["Pick an amount you could manage on your worst day (even a few lines) and a time you are already awake.","Read it in your own language beside the Arabic, so that the reading is not only sound."],"q":[[17,106,106],[35,29,30],[29,45,45],[2,121,121]],"h":[17,18,19],"f":["understanding_what_you_read","reading_arabic_when_hard","laziness_and_discipline"],"m":false,"w":["quran","quran","quran","qur'an","quraan","koran","kuran","mushaf","the quran","reading quran","read quran","quran reading","how to read quran","start reading quran","i want to start reading quran","reading quran consistently","quran every day","daily quran","how much quran should i read","quran habit","finish the quran","wird","juz a day","القرآن","قرآن","قراءة القرآن","ورد القرآن","koran lesen","quran lesen","taglich koran lesen","lire le coran","lecture du coran","membaca quran","baca quran","tilawah","читать коран","чтение корана","kuran okumak","her gun kuran okumak","قرآن پڑھنا","روزانہ قرآن","تلاوت"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"understanding_what_you_read","k":1,"t":"Understanding What You Read","s":"Reading, and understanding none of it","e":"Reading the Arabic and understanding none of it is not a failure. It is where almost everyone begins, and the Qur’an asks to be reflected upon, which means it expects to be worked at rather than absorbed. Explaining a verse is tafsir, a discipline with its own scholars, and inventing it would be worse than leaving it alone. What you get here is the verse itself, in the translation you chose, and the honest advice to take a question you cannot settle to somebody qualified rather than to a search engine.","a":["Read the meaning of a passage first and the Arabic second. Understanding tends to hold attention better than sound alone.","Write down the one verse you did not understand and ask a teacher about that verse, rather than reading a page of guesses."],"q":[[47,24,24],[20,114,114],[38,29,29],[16,43,43]],"h":[20],"f":["reflecting_on_the_quran","asking_a_person_of_knowledge","seeking_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["quran","qur'an","quraan","koran","kuran","mushaf","القرآن","قرآن","understand the quran","understanding the quran","i dont understand the quran","i don't understand the quran","i dont understand what i read","read quran but understand nothing","what does this verse mean","meaning of the verses","meaning of the quran","tafsir","tafseer","commentary on the quran","explain the quran","translation of the quran","فهم القرآن","تفسير","معنى الآيات","koran verstehen","bedeutung der verse","tafsir","comprendre le coran","sens des versets","exegese","memahami quran","arti ayat","tafsir quran","понять коран","смысл аятов","тафсир","kuran anlamak","ayetlerin manasi","tefsir","قرآن سمجھنا","آیات کا مطلب","تفسیر"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"reading_arabic_when_hard","k":1,"t":"When the Arabic Is Hard","s":"Reading slowly, or stumbling","e":"If you read slowly, get words wrong, and would rather not read aloud in front of anyone, you are in the position the Sunnah singles out for encouragement rather than correction. Nobody was born reciting. The Qur’an is described as having been made easy to remember, which is something said about the Book, not a verdict on how quickly you are getting there.","a":["Learn from a person rather than a page. A teacher or a study circle hears the mistakes you cannot hear yourself.","Read three lines slowly and well instead of a page badly. Speed is the last thing to arrive, and it arrives on its own."],"q":[[54,17,17],[73,4,4],[25,32,32]],"h":[21],"f":["reading_the_quran_daily","listening_to_the_quran","laziness_and_discipline"],"m":false,"w":["quran","qur'an","quraan","koran","kuran","mushaf","القرآن","قرآن","cant read arabic","cannot read arabic","i cant read arabic","i can't read arabic","arabic is too hard","arabic is hard","reading arabic is difficult","i stumble when i read","i read slowly","slow at reading quran","learn to read quran","learning arabic letters","noorani qaida","qaida","i make mistakes reading quran","embarrassed to read out loud","لا أستطيع قراءة العربية","القراءة صعبة","تعلم قراءة القرآن","kann kein arabisch lesen","arabisch ist schwer","je ne sais pas lire l arabe","l arabe est difficile","tidak bisa baca arab","susah baca quran","belajar baca quran","не умею читать по арабски","трудно читать коран","arapca okuyamiyorum","kuran okumayi ogrenmek","عربی نہیں پڑھ سکتا","قرآن پڑھنا سیکھنا"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"reflecting_on_the_quran","k":1,"t":"Reflecting Rather Than Finishing","s":"Slowing down with the Qur’an","e":"There is a kind of reading that covers ground and leaves nothing behind, and most of us can tell while we are doing it. Reflection is not a technique, and not a feeling you have to summon before you are allowed to start. It is stopping at the verse that stopped you, and staying there. One ayah you actually thought about is not a smaller thing than a juz you got through.","a":["Stop at the first verse that catches you, read it three times, and go no further today.","Stay with one short surah for a week rather than reading somewhere new each day."],"q":[[4,82,82],[38,29,29],[17,109,109],[59,21,21]],"h":[],"f":["understanding_what_you_read","weak_faith_returning_to_allah","reading_the_quran_daily"],"m":false,"w":["tadabbur","tadabur","reflect on the quran","reflecting on the quran","reflection on the quran","pondering the quran","i feel nothing when i read quran","quran doesnt move me","feel distant from the quran","distant from the quran","rushing through the quran","reading too fast","quran feels empty","how to slow down reading quran","التدبر","تدبر القرآن","الخشوع في القراءة","uber den koran nachdenken","koran betrachten","mediter le coran","reflechir sur le coran","tadabbur quran","merenungkan quran","размышление над кораном","тадаббур","kuran uzerinde dusunmek","tefekkur","قرآن پر غور","تدبر قرآن"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"forgetting_memorisation","k":1,"t":"Memorisation Slipping Away","s":"Forgetting what you memorised","e":"Losing memorised Qur’an happens quietly and is one of the most discouraging things there is. It is not a sin you are being punished for. What is reported about it is a warning about how easily it slips and an instruction to keep returning to it, which describes every hafiz who ever lived, rather than accusing you. Revision is not a penalty for having forgotten. It is simply the work.","a":["Revise what you already hold before adding anything new, even if that means adding nothing for a while.","Recite what you have memorised inside your prayers, where it is revised daily without needing a separate sitting."],"q":[[54,17,17],[25,32,32],[20,114,114]],"h":[22],"f":["reading_the_quran_daily","laziness_and_discipline","guilt_and_shame"],"m":false,"w":["quran","qur'an","quraan","koran","kuran","mushaf","القرآن","قرآن","hifz","hifdh","hifz revision","revising hifz","revision of hifz","memorising quran","memorizing quran","memorisation","memorization","i forgot my memorisation","i forgot my memorization","forgot my hifz","forgetting what i memorised","forgetting what i memorized","losing my hifz","i lost my hifz","cant remember what i memorised","hafiz forgetting","murajaah","muraja'ah","حفظ","نسيت الحفظ","مراجعة الحفظ","تعاهدوا القرآن","koran memorieren","hifz vergessen","wiederholung hifz","memoriser le coran","j ai oublie ma memorisation","hafalan quran","lupa hafalan","muraja'ah hafalan","заучивание корана","забыл выученное","hafizlik","hafizligimi unuttum","ezberi tekrar","حفظ قرآن","حفظ بھول گیا","دہرائی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"listening_to_the_quran","k":1,"t":"Listening and Reciting","s":"Listening, and how you recite","e":"Listening is not a lesser version of reading. The Prophet ﷺ asked a companion to recite to him and wept as he listened, which is the strongest instance there is of the thing you are asking about. Recitation itself is learned by ear: no written description of tajweed will fix a sound you cannot yet hear, and this is one of the few parts of the religion that genuinely cannot be learned from an app.","a":["Stay with one reciter long enough to learn a passage by ear, rather than moving between many.","Have someone qualified listen to you read aloud. Tajweed is corrected by an ear, not by a page."],"q":[[7,204,204],[73,4,4],[17,109,109]],"h":[23],"f":["reading_arabic_when_hard","reflecting_on_the_quran","asking_a_person_of_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["listen to quran","listening to quran","quran audio","quran recitation","recitation","reciter","which reciter","best reciter","beautiful recitation","qari","improve my recitation","improve my tajweed","tajweed","tajwid","how to recite properly","tarteel","tartil","الاستماع للقرآن","التلاوة","التجويد","قارئ","koran horen","koran rezitation","tadschwid","ecouter le coran","recitation du coran","tajwid","mendengarkan quran","murottal","tajwid quran","слушать коран","чтец корана","таджвид","kuran dinlemek","kuran tilaveti","tecvid","قرآن سننا","تلاوت سننا","تجوید"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"sajdah_when_reciting","k":1,"t":"The Prostration Mark While Reading","s":"Reaching a sajdah verse (۩)","e":"The small ۩ in the margin marks a verse at which prostration is reported. The Prophet ﷺ prostrated at such verses and those sitting with him prostrated too. Whether it is required or recommended is a question the schools of law answer differently. ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab said from the pulpit that whoever prostrates has done right and that there is no sin on one who does not. So prostrate when you are able to. If you are somewhere you cannot, keep reading, and take the detailed ruling to someone qualified rather than to a comment thread.","a":["When you reach the mark and are able to, prostrate once, then carry on reading from where you were.","If you cannot prostrate at that moment, keep reading. Ask a person of knowledge what is required in the school you follow."],"q":[[17,109,109],[32,15,15],[96,19,19],[53,62,62],[84,20,21],[19,58,58]],"h":[24,25,26],"f":["asking_a_person_of_knowledge","dua_in_sujood","reading_the_quran_daily"],"m":false,"w":["sajdah","sajda","sajdah verse","sajda verse","sajdah symbol","sajdah sign","sajdah mark","prostration verse","sujud al tilawah","sujood al tilawah","sajdah tilawah","sajdah e tilawat","prostration of recitation","sujood","sujud","sajood","prostration","prostrating","do i have to prostrate","when to prostrate while reading","سجدة","سجود","سجدة التلاوة","آية سجدة","niederwerfung beim lesen","sadschda","prosternation de recitation","verset de prosternation","sujud tilawah","ayat sajdah","sujud saat membaca","земной поклон при чтении","саджда","tilavet secdesi","secde ayeti","secde","سجدہ","سجدہ تلاوت","آیت سجدہ"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"doing_good_unnoticed","k":2,"t":"When Your Good Goes Unnoticed","s":"Doing right when nobody thanks you","e":"“Is the reward for good anything but good?” is often quoted as though people will repay your kindness. They may not. The verse sits in Surah Ar-Rahman among the bounties Allah Himself gives, and the reward it speaks of is His, which is why your effort is not wasted when nobody notices it, and not lost when it is thrown back at you.","a":["Do the next one without telling anyone, and let that be the whole point.","Ask Allah to accept it, rather than asking people to notice it."],"q":[[55,60,60],[76,9,9],[2,110,110],[99,7,7],[4,40,40],[18,30,30]],"h":[27,28],"f":["low_self_worth","feeling_unloved","gratitude"],"m":false,"w":["nobody appreciates me","no one appreciates me","nobody notices","no one notices what i do","my kindness was wasted","my kindness was not returned","always the one giving","why should i be good","why should i keep doing good","why should i continue doing good","tired of being the good one","i am tired of doing the right thing","does allah see my effort","does allah see me","allah does not see me","allah doesn't see my effort","taken for granted","ungrateful people","ihsan","ihsaan","doing good without recognition","good deeds unnoticed","will allah reward me","reward for good","إحسان","الإحسان","was ist ihsan","niemand schaetzt mich","personne ne m'apprecie","qu'est-ce que l'ihsan","tidak ada yang menghargai","apa itu ihsan","меня никто не ценит","что такое ихсан","kimse beni takdir etmiyor","ihsan nedir","کوئی قدر نہیں کرتا","احسان کیا ہے"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"anxiety_and_worry","k":2,"t":"Anxiety and Worry","s":"Feeling anxious or overwhelmed","e":"The Qur’an states plainly that hearts find rest in the remembrance of Allah, not as a quick fix, but as something to return to again and again. The Prophet ﷺ sought refuge from worry and grief by name, so this is not a failure of faith. Alongside that, get whatever practical help you need.","a":["Return to short, simple dhikr when your mind is racing: even a few words, repeated.","If the anxiety is persistent or overwhelming, speak with a qualified professional too. Seeking that help is not a lack of faith."],"q":[[13,28,28],[70,19,22],[2,286,286],[94,5,6]],"h":[29,30],"f":["tawakkul_trust_in_allah","fear_of_the_future","hardship_and_patience"],"m":false,"w":["anxiety","anxious","worried","worry","overthinking","panic","stressed","stress","can't stop worrying","قلق","overwhelmed","overwhelmed","burnout","burnt out","burned out","angst","sorgen","unruhe","anxiete","anxiété","angoisse","inquietude","inquiétude","cemas","gelisah","khawatir","тревога","беспокойство","паника","kaygi","kaygı","endise","endişe","پریشانی","بے چینی"],"d":[1,4,3],"l":"en"},{"id":"sadness_and_grief","k":2,"t":"Sadness and Grief","s":"Feeling low or grieving","e":"Ya‘qub ﷺ said he complains of his grief only to Allah. Grief itself was never the failing. The Qur’an gives glad tidings to the patient and teaches the words said at loss. Feel it, say them, and do not carry it alone.","a":["Let yourself feel it, and say the words the Qur’an teaches at loss.","Tell one person you trust today. Grief kept entirely private grows heavier, not lighter.","If the low mood has lasted for weeks, or is stopping you from sleeping, eating or getting through the day, speak to a doctor too. Seeking treatment is not a lack of faith."],"q":[[2,155,157],[12,86,86],[93,3,5],[39,53,53]],"h":[30],"f":["hope_in_allah","bereavement_and_death","loneliness"],"m":false,"w":["sad","sadness","grief","grieving","grieving a loss","feeling down","feeling low","feeling really low","depressed","depression","i have depression","low mood","mental health","الاكتئاب","depressionen","dépression","depresi","депрессия","depresyon","ڈپریشن","i cant stop crying","i cant stop","cant stop crying","can't stop crying","crying","i keep crying","حزن","traurig","trauer","traurigkeit","tristesse","chagrin","je suis triste","sedih","kesedihan","berduka","печаль","грусть","горе","uzuntu","üzüntü","hüzün","اداسی","دل شکستہ"],"d":[1,12],"l":"en"},{"id":"loneliness","k":2,"t":"Loneliness","s":"Feeling alone","e":"In the cave, the Prophet ﷺ reassured his companion that Allah is with them. Allah’s nearness does not depend on who else is in the room. That is real, and it is also true that you were made for company, so reach for one person this week.","a":["Reach out to one person today, even briefly. A message counts.","Say what you are feeling to Allah directly, out loud if you can. He is not far."],"q":[[9,40,40],[50,16,16],[2,186,186]],"h":[],"f":["feeling_unloved","sadness_and_grief","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["lonely","loneliness","alone","isolated","no friends","nobody understands me","وحدة","einsam","einsamkeit","solitude","je me sens seul","kesepian","sendirian","одиночество","одинок","yalnizlik","yalnızlık","تنہائی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"anger","k":2,"t":"Anger","s":"Struggling to control anger","e":"The Qur’an names restraining anger and pardoning people together, as one habit rather than two. The Prophet ﷺ said strength is holding yourself in that moment, which means the moment is where the work is, not afterwards.","a":["Change your position before you respond: sit if standing, lie down if sitting.","Say a short istighfar or seek refuge from Shaytan before you speak or act."],"q":[[3,134,134],[41,34,34],[7,200,200]],"h":[31],"f":["conflict_and_reconciliation","forgiving_someone","forgiveness_and_repentance"],"m":false,"w":["angry","anger","rage","temper","lost my temper","i get angry","غضب","wut","zorn","colere","colère","marah","amarah","гнев","злость","ofke","öfke","sinir","غصہ"],"d":[13],"l":"en"},{"id":"envy_and_jealousy","k":2,"t":"Envy and Comparison","s":"Comparing yourself to others","e":"The Qur’an tells believers not to wish for what Allah has given others, and separately tells the Prophet ﷺ not to strain his eyes toward what others were given. Envy is treated as a wound to be closed, not a character verdict.","a":["Make du‘a for the person you envy, by name. It is difficult, and it works on the heart.","Name one blessing of your own you have stopped noticing, and thank Allah for it."],"q":[[4,32,32],[113,1,5],[20,131,131]],"h":[],"f":["gratitude","feeling_behind_in_life","seeking_protection"],"m":false,"w":["envy","jealous","jealousy","hasad","comparing myself","everyone else is ahead","حسد","neid","eifersucht","jalousie","envie","iri","dengki","cemburu","зависть","ревность","kiskanclik","kıskançlık","haset","حسد کرنا","رشک"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"gratitude","k":2,"t":"Gratitude","s":"Being grateful to Allah","e":"The Qur’an promises increase for the grateful. Gratitude here is a practice more than a feeling: said in words, shown in worship, and visible in how a blessing is used.","a":["Name three specific blessings today, and thank Allah for them by name.","Before you sleep, thank Allah for what fed and sheltered you today, in your own words or in the words below."],"q":[[14,7,7],[2,152,152],[16,18,18],[31,12,12]],"h":[28],"f":["contentment_with_qadr","hope_in_allah","envy_and_jealousy"],"m":false,"w":["thank allah","thanking allah","how to thank allah","being thankful","dua for gratitude","remercier allah","bersyukur kepada allah","благодарить аллаха","allaha sukur","allah'a şükür","اللہ کا شکر","gratitude","grateful","thankful","blessings","counting my blessings","shukr","alhamdulillah","شكر","dankbarkeit","dankbar","gratitude envers allah","reconnaissance","syukur","bersyukur","благодарность","sukur","şükür","شکر"],"d":[14,15],"l":"en"},{"id":"low_self_worth","k":2,"t":"Feeling Worthless","s":"You do not feel good enough","e":"Allah says He honoured the children of Adam and created the human being in the best form. Your worth was not issued by the people who withheld it, and it is not cancelled by what you have failed at. What Allah measures is taqwa, and that is still in front of you.","a":["Do one small good deed nobody will see today. Worth is built where nobody is watching.","If these thoughts are constant, speak to someone you trust and to a qualified professional."],"q":[[17,70,70],[95,4,4],[49,13,13]],"h":[32],"f":["feeling_unloved","guilt_and_shame","feeling_behind_in_life"],"m":false,"w":["worthless","i feel worthless","self worth","self esteem","i hate myself","not good enough","i am useless","no confidence","احتقار الذات","wertlos","selbstwert","sans valeur","estime de soi","tidak berharga","harga diri","никчемный","самооценка","degersizim","değersizim","ozguven","özgüven","بے وقعت","خود اعتمادی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"feeling_unloved","k":2,"t":"Feeling Unloved","s":"Nobody seems to want you","e":"In Surah ad-Duha, Allah tells the Prophet ﷺ directly that his Lord has neither left him nor turned away from him, revealed at a moment when it looked exactly as though He had. Silence is not abandonment.","a":["Ask Allah for what you are missing, in plain words. Naming it to Him is allowed.","Give the kindness you are waiting for to one other person this week."],"q":[[93,3,5],[50,16,16],[2,186,186],[39,53,53]],"h":[],"f":["loneliness","low_self_worth","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["nobody loves me","i feel unloved","allah doesn't love me","unwanted","feel forgotten","abandoned","does allah love me","لا احد يحبني","ungeliebt","niemand liebt mich","personne ne m aime","mal aime","mal aimé","tidak dicintai","tidak ada yang sayang","меня никто не любит","ненужный","kimse beni sevmiyor","sevilmiyorum","کوئی مجھ سے محبت نہیں کرتا"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"guilt_and_shame","k":2,"t":"Guilt and Shame","s":"You cannot forgive yourself","e":"Guilt that moves you to return is doing its work. Guilt that convinces you the door is closed is not. The Qur’an addresses that exact despair and forbids it. You are not the first person to need this verse.","a":["Make tawbah once, sincerely, and then stop reopening the case against yourself.","If you wronged a person, put right what can be put right, quietly."],"q":[[39,53,53],[2,222,222],[66,8,8],[7,23,23]],"h":[33],"f":["forgiveness_and_repentance","returning_to_the_same_sin","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["guilt","guilty","ashamed","shame","i feel guilty","can't forgive myself","i cant forgive myself","regret","haunted by what i did","ذنب","خجل","ندم","schuld","scham","culpabilite","culpabilité","honte","rasa bersalah","malu","вина","стыд","suclu hissetmek","suçlu hissetmek","utanc","utanç","شرمندگی","احساس جرم"],"d":[16,17],"l":"en"},{"id":"heartbreak","k":2,"t":"Heartbreak","s":"Losing someone you wanted","e":"The pain is real, and the Qur’an does not ask you to pretend otherwise. It says only that you may hate a thing that is good for you, and that you do not see what Allah sees. Grieve it honestly, and do not build your worth on a door that closed.","a":["Tell Allah exactly how much it hurts. Ya‘qub did, and the Qur’an recorded it.","Keep your prayers and your sleep. Grief is heaviest on a body that has stopped being cared for."],"q":[[12,86,86],[2,216,216],[94,5,6],[65,2,3]],"h":[30],"f":["sadness_and_grief","contentment_with_qadr","betrayal_and_broken_trust"],"m":false,"w":["heartbreak","heartbroken","broken heart","breakup","broke up","she left me","he left me","rejected","lost the person i loved","قلب مكسور","انكسار القلب","liebeskummer","herzschmerz","chagrin d amour","coeur brise","cœur brisé","patah hati","putus cinta","разбитое сердце","расставание","kalp kirikligi","kalp kırıklığı","ayrilik","ayrılık","دل ٹوٹنا"],"d":[1,3],"l":"en"},{"id":"prophets_who_struggled","k":3,"t":"The Prophets Felt It Too","s":"Fear, grief and loneliness in the lives of the prophets","e":"If you believe your grief is evidence of weak faith, the Qur’an says otherwise. Ya‘qub complained of his sorrow, and he complained of it to Allah. Ayyub named his adversity out loud. Yunus called out from the darkness. The feeling was never the failure; where they took it is what the Qur’an records.","a":["Say the thing you cannot say to anyone else to Allah, in your own words.","Notice where you take the feeling, rather than judging yourself for having it."],"q":[[12,86,86],[21,83,83],[21,87,87],[93,3,3],[18,6,6],[19,23,23],[94,5,6]],"h":[34],"f":["purpose_of_tests","sadness_and_grief","what_ummahti_means"],"m":false,"w":["did the prophets struggle","did prophets feel sad","did the prophets feel fear","did prophets get lonely","prophets suffering","prophets tested","tested the most","why am i being tested","am i weak for feeling this","wrong to feel sad","yaqub grief","yaqub sadness","ayyub illness","story of ayyub","yunus dua","yunus and the fish","maryam pain","prophet muhammad sadness","prophet was sad","has allah abandoned me","allah has left me","i feel abandoned","i cannot bear this","i can't bear this","أشد الناس بلاء","الأنبياء","صبر أيوب","haben die propheten gelitten","les prophetes ont-ils souffert","apakah para nabi menderita","страдали ли пророки","peygamberler de zorlandi mi","کیا انبیاء نے تکلیف اٹھائی"],"d":[18],"l":"en"},{"id":"hardship_and_patience","k":3,"t":"Hardship and Patience","s":"Going through a hard time","e":"The Qur’an repeats a short, striking promise: with hardship comes ease, alongside it, not only after it. The patience it asks for is active, meaning prayer, perseverance and trust, rather than simply waiting it out.","a":["Turn to prayer when it is hardest. The Qur’an pairs patience with prayer directly.","Name the one part of this you can still act on, and act on that part today."],"q":[[94,5,6],[2,153,153],[2,155,157],[39,10,10],[65,7,7]],"h":[28],"f":["purpose_of_tests","tawakkul_trust_in_allah","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["hardship","patience","sabr","hard time","difficult time","going through a lot","everything is falling apart","struggling","صبر","schwere zeit","geduld","epreuve","épreuve","moment difficile","kesulitan","sabar","masa sulit","трудности","терпение","тяжелое время","тяжёлое время","zorluk","sabir","sabır","zor zaman","مشکل","کٹھن وقت","صبر کرنا"],"d":[4,3,19,20],"l":"en"},{"id":"purpose_of_tests","k":3,"t":"Why Allah Tests Us","s":"Making sense of what is happening","e":"The Qur’an says life and death were created to test which of us is best in deed, and that saying “we believe” is not left untested. That tells you what tests are for in general. It does not tell you the reason for yours.","a":["Ask what this is asking of you now, rather than why it was sent.","Ask Allah for relief and for good in the outcome, in the same breath."],"q":[[67,2,2],[29,2,3],[21,35,35],[2,155,155]],"h":[35,36],"f":["prophets_who_struggled","hardship_and_patience","contentment_with_qadr","dunya_is_temporary"],"m":false,"w":["why is this happening to me","why does allah test us","why am i being tested","purpose of tests","meaning of suffering","why do good people suffer","is allah punishing me","ابتلاء","لماذا يبتليني الله","warum prufungen","warum prüfungen","pourquoi ces epreuves","pourquoi ces épreuves","kenapa diuji","mengapa allah menguji","почему испытания","за что мне это","neden sinaniyorum","neden sınanıyorum","imtihan neden","آزمائش کیوں"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"contentment_with_qadr","k":3,"t":"Accepting Allah’s Decree","s":"Making peace with what happened","e":"The Qur’an says nothing befalls the earth or yourselves except it is written before it comes about, and gives the reason: so that you do not despair over what escaped you, nor exult over what you were given. Acceptance is not resignation; it is being freed from arguing with the past.","a":["Stop replaying the alternative version. The Prophet ﷺ named “if only” as the door it opens.","Ask Allah to make you content with what He decreed, and to open what comes next."],"q":[[57,22,23],[2,216,216],[64,11,11],[9,51,51]],"h":[3,37],"f":["tawakkul_trust_in_allah","purpose_of_tests","gratitude"],"m":false,"w":["qadr","qadar","accepting fate","accepting allah's decree","destiny","why did this happen","it wasn't meant to be","content with what allah gave","it was not meant to be","meant","meaning","it was not meant to be","not meant to be","what allah wills","qadarallah","qaddarallah","qadarullah wa ma shaa faal","قدر","قضاء وقدر","الرضا بالقدر","schicksal","vorherbestimmung","destin","predestination","prédestination","takdir","menerima takdir","предопределение","судьба","kader","kaza ve kader","تقدیر","قضا و قدر"],"d":[21],"l":"en"},{"id":"failure_and_setbacks","k":3,"t":"Failure and Setbacks","s":"It did not work out","e":"After the hardest day of the early community, the Qur’an said: do not weaken and do not grieve. It was not a denial that they had lost; it was an instruction about what to do next. A setback is information about a route, not a verdict on you.","a":["Write down the one thing you would do differently, then close the review.","Take the next step within your reach today, however small, and leave the outcome with Allah."],"q":[[3,139,139],[94,5,6],[2,216,216],[3,159,159]],"h":[37],"f":["failing_an_exam","feeling_behind_in_life","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["i failed","failure","failed","setback","everything i try fails","i keep failing","my plan failed","rejected again","lost everything","فشل","فشلت","gescheitert","versagt","misserfolg","echec","échec","j ai echoue","j ai échoué","gagal","kegagalan","неудача","провал","basarisiz","başarısız","basarisizlik","başarısızlık","ناکامی","ناکام"],"d":[21],"l":"en"},{"id":"fear_of_the_future","k":3,"t":"Fear of the Future","s":"Not knowing what will happen","e":"Not knowing what comes next is the ordinary human condition, not a fault in you. The Qur’an says plainly that no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow. What it promises is a way out and provision from where you did not expect, for the one who is mindful of Allah.","a":["Deal with what is actually in front of you this week; the rest is not yours to carry yet.","Say “Allah is sufficient for me” when the spiral starts, and then do the next ordinary task."],"q":[[65,2,3],[3,173,173],[31,34,34],[9,51,51]],"h":[37],"f":["tawakkul_trust_in_allah","anxiety_and_worry","contentment_with_qadr"],"m":false,"w":["scared of the future","afraid of the future","uncertainty","uncertain","i don't know what will happen","what if it goes wrong","fear","afraid","everything is unknown","خوف من المستقبل","قلق المستقبل","zukunftsangst","ungewissheit","peur de l avenir","incertitude","takut masa depan","ketidakpastian","страх будущего","неизвестность","gelecek korkusu","belirsizlik","مستقبل کا خوف","بے یقینی"],"d":[22,18],"l":"en"},{"id":"illness_and_healing","k":3,"t":"Illness and Healing","s":"Dua for healing","e":"Ibrahim ﷺ said that when he is ill, it is Allah who cures him, a statement of trust made alongside seeking treatment, never instead of it. Take the medicine and make the du‘a; the Qur’an never set them against each other.","a":["Seek qualified medical care, and make sincere du‘a for shifa alongside it.","Ask others to make du‘a for you. It costs you nothing and is worth more than you think."],"q":[[26,80,80],[21,83,83],[6,17,17]],"h":[36,38],"f":["chronic_illness_and_pain","caring_for_someone_ill","hardship_and_patience"],"m":true,"w":["illness","sick","healing","shifa","disease","unwell","مرض","شفاء","before surgery dua","dua for the sick","dua for someone sick","dua for healing","surgery","before surgery","operation","hospital","in hospital","cancer","covid","in pain","my body hurts","headache","diagnosis","دعاء المريض","دعاء للمريض","مستشفى","عملية جراحية","krankenhaus","dua fur kranke","dua für kranke","hopital","hôpital","dua pour un malade","doa untuk orang sakit","rumah sakit","operasi","больница","операция","дуа для больного","hasta icin dua","hasta için dua","hastane","ameliyat","ہسپتال","مریض کے لیے دعا","krank","krankheit","heilung","malade","maladie","guerison","guérison","sakit","penyakit","kesembuhan","болезнь","болею","исцеление","hastalik","hastalık","şifa","بیماری","بیمار"],"d":[23,24,25],"l":"en"},{"id":"chronic_illness_and_pain","k":3,"t":"Living with Long-Term Illness","s":"Pain that does not lift","e":"Ayyub ﷺ said only that harm had touched him and that Allah is the most merciful: no long complaint, and no pretending. The Prophet ﷺ said nothing reaches a Muslim, even a thorn, without Allah expiating something by it. Your pain is not wasted, and you are allowed to say it is hard.","a":["Keep your treatment plan, and lower what you demand of yourself on the worst days.","Pray as you are able. Sitting or lying down is prayer, not a lesser version of it."],"q":[[21,83,83],[2,286,286],[2,155,157],[94,5,6]],"h":[36,28],"f":["illness_and_healing","hardship_and_patience","contentment_with_qadr"],"m":true,"w":["chronic illness","chronic pain","long term illness","always in pain","i live with pain","disability","incurable","it never goes away","مرض مزمن","الم مزمن","chronische krankheit","chronische schmerzen","maladie chronique","douleur chronique","penyakit kronis","sakit menahun","хроническая болезнь","хроническая боль","kronik hastalik","kronik hastalık","surekli agri","sürekli ağrı","دائمی بیماری","مسلسل درد"],"d":[23,4,25],"l":"en"},{"id":"caring_for_someone_ill","k":3,"t":"Caring for Someone Ill","s":"You are the one holding it together","e":"The Qur’an names those who counsel one another to patience and to compassion as people of the right hand. What you are doing is worship, even when it is unglamorous and nobody thanks you. Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity, which also means your limits are real and may be respected.","a":["Accept one offer of help this week instead of declining it out of habit.","Ask Allah for strength for yourself too, not only healing for them."],"q":[[90,17,17],[2,286,286],[2,153,153],[17,24,24]],"h":[],"f":["illness_and_healing","parents","hardship_and_patience"],"m":true,"w":["looking after someone sick","caring for my mother","caring for my father","carer","caregiver","my parent is ill","my child is ill","burnt out caring","رعاية مريض","pflege","jemanden pflegen","aidant","s occuper d un malade","merawat orang sakit","menjaga orang sakit","уход за больным","hasta bakimi","hasta bakımı","بیمار کی دیکھ بھال"],"d":[26,23,4,27],"l":"en"},{"id":"bereavement_and_death","k":3,"t":"Bereavement and Death","s":"Losing someone","e":"“To Allah we belong, and to Him we return” is said at loss as both truth and comfort. Every soul returns to Allah, and grief is not a failure of faith. The Prophet ﷺ taught words to say through it, not instead of it.","a":["Say the words, and make du‘a for the one who has passed, by name.","Let people who care about you sit with you. You are not required to be strong in public."],"q":[[2,155,157],[3,185,185],[17,24,24]],"h":[39,40,41],"f":["sadness_and_grief","preparing_for_the_akhirah","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["death","someone died","loss","bereavement","grieving","lost someone","my mother died","my mother","janazah","janaza","funeral","funeral prayer","dua for the deceased","dua for the dead","dua for someone who died","what to say when someone dies","inna lillahi","inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajiun","condolences","offering condolences","my","my wife","my wife","My wife died","wife died","mother died","father died","mom died","mum died","dad died","husband died","wife died","child died","son died","daughter died","brother died","sister died","miscarriage","stillbirth","lost my baby","lost a baby","baby died","relative died","relatives died","a relative passed away","صلاة الجنازة","الجنازة","دعاء للميت","العزاء","تعزية","beerdigung","beileid","dua fur verstorbene","dua für verstorbene","funerailles","funérailles","condoleances","condoléances","jenazah","doa untuk orang meninggal","takziah","похороны","джаназа","дуа за умершего","соболезнования","cenaze","cenaze namazi","cenaze namazı","olu icin dua","ölü için dua","taziye","جنازہ","میت کے لیے دعا","تعزیت","passed away","lost my mother","lost my father","lost my child","mom passed away","dad passed away","innalillah","موت","وفاة","todesfall","trauerfall","deuil","deces","décès","kematian","meninggal","berduka cita","смерть","утрата","умер","vefat","olum","ölüm","kayip","kayıp","موت","انتقال"],"d":[28,29,27],"l":"en"},{"id":"injustice_and_oppression","k":3,"t":"Injustice and Being Wronged","s":"Someone wronged you","e":"The Qur’an permits you to defend yourself when wronged, and separately praises patience and forgiveness as matters of resolve. Both are open to you. What is never open is silence in the face of injustice done to somebody weaker.","a":["Pursue a fair, lawful response: through the proper channel, not through revenge.","Make du‘a against the injustice. It is one of the few things nobody can take from you."],"q":[[42,39,39],[4,135,135],[42,43,43]],"h":[42,43],"f":["betrayal_and_broken_trust","forgiving_someone","hardship_and_patience"],"m":false,"w":["injustice","oppression","oppressed","being wronged","treated unfairly","unfair treatment","someone wronged me","bullied","discriminated","ظلم","enemy","enemies","my enemies","dua against enemies","afraid of people","boss is unfair","unfair boss","ungerechtigkeit","unterdruckung","unterdrückung","injustice subie","oppression","ketidakadilan","dizalimi","penindasan","несправедливость","притеснение","haksizlik","haksızlık","zulum","zulüm","ظلم","ناانصافی"],"d":[30],"l":"en"},{"id":"what_ummahti_means","k":4,"t":"What Ummahti Means","s":"The name of this app, and what it asks of you","e":"Ummahti is his word, not ours. With his hands raised the Prophet ﷺ said, “my Ummah, my Ummah”, and wept. In a separate narration he stood before a graveyard and called the believers who had not yet come his brothers, and said he wished he could see them. The Qur’an calls him a mercy sent to the worlds and describes him as grieved by what burdens you. Belonging to this Ummah is not only something you were born into. It asks something of you in return.","a":["Send salawat upon him once, deliberately, before you close this.","Keep one sunnah you already know today, out of love rather than duty."],"q":[[21,107,107],[9,128,128],[42,13,13],[33,21,21],[14,36,36],[5,118,118],[3,31,31],[3,110,110]],"h":[44,45,46,47,48],"f":["prophets_who_struggled","hope_in_allah","forgiveness_and_repentance"],"m":false,"w":["ummahti","what does ummahti mean","meaning of ummahti","ummati","my ummah","ummah","what is the ummah","what is special about this ummah","why is the app called ummahti","the name of this app","prophet cares about us","why does the prophet care about us","did the prophet know about us","prophet wept for his ummah","prophet cried for his ummah","prophet love for ummah","how do i love the prophet","how to follow the prophet","love for the prophet","following the sunnah with love","what did musa do for this ummah","musa and the prayers","why five prayers","intercession","shafaah","shafa'ah","أمتي","امتي","الأمة","شفاعة","meine umma","was bedeutet ummahti","ma oumma","que signifie ummahti","umatku","apa arti ummahti","моя умма","что значит уммахти","ummetim","ummahti ne demek","میری امت","امت"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"forgiveness_and_repentance","k":4,"t":"Forgiveness and Repentance","s":"I sinned. Will Allah forgive me?","e":"Do not let the sin make you despair of Allah’s mercy. That is the Qur’an’s own instruction, addressed to people who thought they had gone too far. Sincere tawbah is remorse, stopping, and a real intention not to return. No recitation replaces that turning, and nothing you did closes the door on it.","a":["Make tawbah now, in your own words: remorse, stopping, and a real intention not to return.","Follow the wrong action with a good one; the Qur’an describes good deeds as removing bad ones."],"q":[[39,53,53],[4,110,110],[66,8,8],[42,25,25],[3,135,135]],"h":[49,33],"f":["returning_to_the_same_sin","guilt_and_shame","hope_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["sinned","i sinned","forgiveness","repent","repentance","tawbah","tawba","istighfar","will allah forgive me","i did something bad","guilty","guilt","astaghfirullah","astagfirullah","allah will not forgive me","allah wont forgive me","allah will never forgive me","i am beyond forgiveness","unforgivable","my sins are too many","توبة","استغفار","مغفرة","vergebung","gesundigt","gesündigt","sunde","sünde","repentir","pardon","se repentir","peche","péché","taubat","tobat","ampunan","berbuat dosa","покаяние","прощение","согрешил","tovbe","tövbe","tevbe","gunah","günah","توبہ","گناہ","معافی"],"d":[16,17,31],"l":"en"},{"id":"returning_to_the_same_sin","k":4,"t":"Falling Back into the Same Sin","s":"You keep breaking your own tawbah","e":"In a narration of the Prophet ﷺ, a servant sins, repents, and sins again, and each time Allah forgives him, because he knew he had a Lord who forgives. The Qur’an praises those who do not persist knowingly; it does not say they never fall. The measure is the returning, not the record.","a":["Repent again, without treating the last tawbah as wasted. It was not.","Change one thing about the situation that makes it easy, not just your intention about it."],"q":[[3,135,135],[39,53,53],[4,110,110],[13,11,11]],"h":[50,49],"f":["breaking_a_harmful_habit","forgiveness_and_repentance","guilt_and_shame"],"m":false,"w":["i keep sinning","same sin again","i did it again","keep going back to the sin","relapsed","i can't stop sinning","i cant stop sinning","repeated sin","my tawbah keeps breaking","اكرر نفس الذنب","اعود للذنب","immer wieder sundigen","immer wieder sündigen","ruckfall","rückfall","je retombe dans le peche","je retombe dans le péché","rechute","mengulangi dosa","kembali berbuat dosa","снова согрешил","повторяю грех","ayni gunahi tekrarliyorum","aynı günahı tekrarlıyorum","بار بار گناہ"],"d":[16,32],"l":"en"},{"id":"breaking_a_harmful_habit","k":4,"t":"Breaking a Harmful Habit","s":"Something you cannot seem to stop","e":"The Qur’an says Allah does not change a people until they change what is in themselves, and promises guidance to those who strive. Strive means the practical work as well as the du‘a: change the circumstances, not only the resolve. The Prophet ﷺ warned against overwhelming yourself, so set a step you can actually keep.","a":["Remove one thing that makes it easy: the app, the route home, the hour you are alone.","Tell one trustworthy person, or get professional help if it is an addiction. Secrecy is what keeps it alive."],"q":[[13,11,11],[29,69,69],[2,286,286],[7,200,200]],"h":[1,37],"f":["returning_to_the_same_sin","laziness_and_discipline","protection_from_whispers"],"m":false,"w":["addiction","addicted","bad habit","harmful habit","break a habit","i can't stop","i cant stop","quit","quitting","porn","smoking","wasting my life on my phone","ادمان","عادة سيئة","sucht","schlechte angewohnheit","addiction","mauvaise habitude","dependance","dépendance","kecanduan","kebiasaan buruk","зависимость","вредная привычка","bagimlilik","bağımlılık","kotu aliskanlik","kötü alışkanlık","لت","بری عادت"],"d":[1,16],"l":"en"},{"id":"weak_faith_returning_to_allah","k":4,"t":"Weak Faith, Returning to Allah","s":"Feeling distant from Allah","e":"Faith rises and falls for everyone; the return matters more than never having drifted. The Qur’an asks directly whether the time has not come for hearts to soften at Allah’s remembrance. That is a question, not a dismissal, and it is asked of believers.","a":["Start with one small, consistent act today: a prayer on time, a page of Qur’an.","Sit with people whose company makes worship easier for you, even once this month."],"q":[[39,53,53],[42,25,25],[57,16,16],[29,69,69]],"h":[1],"f":["missing_salah","doubts_and_waswas","laziness_and_discipline"],"m":false,"w":["weak faith","weak iman","losing faith","losing my faith","strengthen my iman","strengthen iman","coming back to allah","returning to allah","i feel far from allah","my iman is low","spiritually empty","إيمان","ضعف الايمان","schwacher glaube","glauben verloren","foi faible","je perds la foi","iman lemah","futur iman","jauh dari allah","слабая вера","теряю веру","imani zayif","imanı zayıf","allahtan uzak","کمزور ایمان","اللہ سے دوری"],"d":[33],"l":"en"},{"id":"doubts_and_waswas","k":4,"t":"Doubts and Whispered Thoughts","s":"Thoughts you did not choose","e":"A thought that arrives uninvited and horrifies you is not your belief; your distress at it is itself evidence of your faith. The Qur’an’s instruction for a whisper is to seek refuge in Allah and move on, not to argue the thought down. A settled question is best taken to a person of knowledge.","a":["Do not debate the thought. Seek refuge, and deliberately turn to something else.","If a real question is troubling you, take it to a person of knowledge rather than to the internet."],"q":[[7,200,200],[3,8,8],[23,97,98],[41,36,36]],"h":[],"f":["protection_from_whispers","weak_faith_returning_to_allah","seeking_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["doubts","doubt","i have doubts about islam","questioning my faith","waswas","waswasa","shubuhat","blasphemous thoughts","scary thoughts about allah","شك","شكوك","وسواس","zweifel","glaubenszweifel","doutes","je doute","keraguan","ragu","сомнения","сомневаюсь","supheler","şüpheler","vesvese","شکوک","وسوسہ"],"d":[33],"l":"en"},{"id":"protection_from_whispers","k":4,"t":"Protection from Whispers","s":"Intrusive thoughts and whispers","e":"The Qur’an’s own instruction for an evil suggestion is to seek refuge in Allah, not to argue with the thought, but to turn away from it toward Him. Surah an-Nas closes the Qur’an on exactly this, which tells you how ordinary it is.","a":["Say a short phrase seeking refuge, and turn your attention elsewhere at once.","Read the last two surahs of the Qur’an in the morning and the evening."],"q":[[7,200,200],[114,1,6],[23,97,98],[16,98,98]],"h":[],"f":["doubts_and_waswas","seeking_protection","before_sleeping"],"m":false,"w":["whispers","waswasa","shaytan whispers","protection from shaytan","intrusive thoughts","bad thoughts","وسواس","وساوس الشيطان","einflusterungen","einflüsterungen","aufdringliche gedanken","chuchotements","pensees intrusives","pensées intrusives","bisikan syaitan","pikiran buruk","наущения","навязчивые мысли","vesvese","seytan vesvesesi","şeytan vesvesesi","وسوسے","برے خیالات"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"hope_in_allah","k":4,"t":"Hope in Allah","s":"Feeling that it is too late","e":"The Qur’an addresses those who feel furthest from hope directly: do not despair of Allah’s mercy. It is a command, not merely a comfort, and it was said to people who genuinely believed they had gone too far.","a":["Read this verse slowly, and take its command seriously. Hope in Allah’s mercy is not optional.","Do one act of worship today as a way back, however small it looks to you."],"q":[[39,53,53],[12,87,87],[93,3,5],[94,5,6]],"h":[51,52,49],"f":["guilt_and_shame","weak_faith_returning_to_allah","sadness_and_grief"],"m":false,"w":["hope","hopeless","despair","raja","no hope left","i have given up","gone too far","رجاء","يأس","hoffnung","hoffnungslos","verzweiflung","espoir","desespoir","désespoir","harapan","putus asa","надежда","отчаяние","umit","ümit","umutsuzluk","امید","مایوسی"],"d":[3,16],"l":"en"},{"id":"new_to_islam","k":4,"t":"New to Islam","s":"Beginning, or beginning again","e":"There is more to learn than anyone could learn this month, and trying to do all of it at once is the most common reason people stop. ‘Amr ibn al-‘As accepted Islam having wanted to kill the Prophet ﷺ, and asked to be pardoned as a condition, and was told that Islam wipes out what came before it. You are not behind. Learn the five prayers, pray them imperfectly, and let the rest arrive in its own order.","a":["Learn the five prayers first, and pray them badly rather than not at all. The rest can wait its turn.","Find one teacher and one community you can actually ask questions of. Learning alone is slower and much lonelier."],"q":[[2,286,286],[94,5,6],[16,43,43]],"h":[53,17,1],"f":["asking_a_person_of_knowledge","reading_the_quran_daily","seeking_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["new muslim","new to islam","i just became muslim","learn to pray","learning to pray","learning to pray salah","teach me salah","teach me how to pray","i dont know how to pray","i don't know how to pray","how to pray salah","how to perform salah","how to do salah","i became muslim","revert","reverted","convert to islam","converted to islam","i took shahada","shahada","just accepted islam","starting islam","beginner muslim","where do i even start","what do i learn first","coming back after years","practising again after years","مسلم جديد","أسلمت حديثا","من أين أبدأ","neuer muslim","gerade muslim geworden","konvertit","nouveau musulman","je viens de me convertir","converti","muslim baru","baru masuk islam","mualaf","новый мусульманин","принял ислам","с чего начать","yeni musluman","yeni müslüman","ihtida","nereden baslamaliyim","نیا مسلمان","کہاں سے شروع کروں"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"marriage_finding_spouse","k":5,"t":"Marriage and Finding a Spouse","s":"Seeking a righteous spouse","e":"The Qur’an describes marriage as a source of tranquility, not a prize won by a formula. Sincere effort, honest du‘a and patience with Allah’s timing sit together, and no verse promises a spouse by a set date. Your worth is not on hold until this happens.","a":["Make sincere du‘a for a righteous spouse, in your own words, at any time.","Take real, permissible steps: ask people you trust, and consider istikharah for a specific decision."],"q":[[30,21,21],[25,74,74],[24,32,32]],"h":[],"f":["decision_making_istikhara","feeling_behind_in_life","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["marriage","getting married","find a spouse","find a wife","find a husband","looking for a wife","looking for a husband","marry","marry someone","want to marry","nikah","nikkah","rishta","rishtay","marraige","when will i get married","can't find someone to marry","زواج","نكاح","Ehe","rehearse","heiraten","heirat","ehepartner","mariage","me marier","se marier","menikah","pernikahan","jodoh","жениться","выйти замуж","брак","evlilik","evlenmek","شادی","رشتہ","شادی کرنا"],"d":[34],"l":"en"},{"id":"marital_relationship","k":5,"t":"Living Well Together","s":"Being a good spouse day to day","e":"A marriage is built on tranquility, mercy and patient kindness, not on getting every day right. The Qur’an calls spouses a garment for one another: closeness, covering and protection, in ordinary daily terms.","a":["Choose one kind, patient word or action today, and revisit conflict when you are both calm.","Pray for your spouse by name, in your own words and in the words below."],"q":[[30,21,21],[4,19,19],[2,187,187]],"h":[],"f":["marriage_difficulty","conflict_and_reconciliation","gratitude"],"m":false,"w":["wedding","wedding dua","newlywed","newlyweds","newly married","just got married","dua for newly married couple","barakallahu laka","barakallahu lakuma","dua for my husband","dua for my wife","dua for my spouse","دعاء للعروسين","بارك الله لكما","hochzeit","frisch verheiratet","jeunes maries","jeunes mariés","pengantin baru","doa pengantin","свадьба","молодожены","dugun duasi","düğün duası","yeni evliler","دولہا دلہن کے لیے دعا","married life","husband and wife","spouse relationship","married couple","being a good husband","being a good wife","زوج","زوجة"],"d":[34,35,36],"l":"en"},{"id":"marriage_difficulty","k":5,"t":"When a Marriage Is in Trouble","s":"Serious conflict at home","e":"The Qur’an’s own instruction when a couple fears a breach is to appoint an arbitrator from each family. Bring wise people in rather than fight it out alone. It also says reconciliation is better. A trusted counsellor or scholar can help with your specific case. If there is harm or abuse, your safety comes first.","a":["Bring in a trusted, qualified person from each side, as the Qur’an instructs.","If there is harm or abuse, get to safety first and seek help. Patience never means enduring harm."],"q":[[4,35,35],[4,128,128],[4,19,19],[65,2,3]],"h":[],"f":["marital_relationship","conflict_and_reconciliation","anger"],"m":false,"w":["marriage problems","marital issues","my marriage is failing","my husband ignores me","my wife ignores me","fighting with my husband","fighting with my wife","divorce","talaq","unhappy marriage","marriage is hard","مشاكل زوجية","طلاق","eheprobleme","scheidung","problemes de couple","problèmes de couple","divorce","masalah rumah tangga","cerai","perceraian","проблемы в браке","развод","evlilik sorunlari","evlilik sorunları","bosanma","boşanma","ازدواجی مسائل","طلاق"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"parents","k":5,"t":"Parents","s":"Being good to parents","e":"Kindness to parents is named beside the worship of Allah Himself, with a specific instruction against even a word of contempt. That is a very high and very concrete standard, and it is met in small daily things far more often than in grand gestures.","a":["Do one concrete thing for your parents today, and make du‘a for them by name."],"q":[[17,23,24],[31,14,14],[46,15,15]],"h":[54],"f":["family_pressure","conflict_and_reconciliation","caring_for_someone_ill"],"m":false,"w":["parents","mother","father","mom","dad","birr al walidayn","والدين","eltern","parents ages","orang tua","родители","anne baba","والدین"],"d":[27],"l":"en"},{"id":"family_pressure","k":5,"t":"Family Pressure","s":"Being pushed toward something","e":"The Qur’an holds two things together in one verse: do not obey parents in disobedience to Allah, and keep their company in this world with kindness. You may decline what is not yours to give and still honour them. Culture and religion are not always the same thing, and telling them apart is the work here.","a":["Say your answer once, clearly and respectfully, and do not argue it again every week.","Ask a person of knowledge whether the demand is religion or custom, before you carry the guilt."],"q":[[31,15,15],[17,23,24],[2,286,286],[65,2,3]],"h":[],"f":["parents","conflict_and_reconciliation","anxiety_and_worry"],"m":false,"w":["family pressure","my family is forcing me","pressure to marry","parents won't let me","cultural pressure","expectations from my family","forced marriage","my parents want me to","ضغط الاهل","ضغط العائلة","familiendruck","druck von der familie","pression familiale","tekanan keluarga","dipaksa keluarga","давление семьи","aile baskisi","aile baskısı","خاندانی دباؤ","گھر والوں کا دباؤ"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"conflict_and_reconciliation","k":5,"t":"Conflict and Reconciliation","s":"Fixing a broken relationship","e":"The Qur’an calls believers brothers and sisters to one another and asks for reconciliation between them, naming the relationship as the reason to repair it. It also says to repel an evil with what is better, so that the one you are at odds with may become close.","a":["Take the first step yourself, even if you feel you were the one wronged.","Say the one sentence you have been withholding, and leave the rest for later."],"q":[[49,10,10],[41,34,34],[4,128,128]],"h":[55],"f":["forgiving_someone","anger","family_pressure"],"m":false,"w":["conflict","family argument","family dispute","dispute","fighting with family","neighbour problems","neighbor problems","problems with neighbours","problems with my neighbor","fighting with my family","arguing with my family","reconcile","reconciling","reconciliation","fell out","not speaking to","صلح","خصام","streit","versohnung","versöhnung","conflit","reconciliation","réconciliation","islah","islam","islam","konflik","berselisih","perselisihan","конфликт","примирение","kavga","barismak","barışmak","جھگڑا","صلح"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"forgiving_someone","k":5,"t":"Forgiving Someone","s":"Letting go of what they did","e":"The Qur’an asks a question rather than issuing a demand: would you not love that Allah should forgive you? Forgiving is not saying it did not matter, and it does not oblige you to restore the relationship. It is choosing to stop carrying the debt.","a":["Decide once that you are no longer collecting the debt, and stop retelling the story.","You may forgive without restoring closeness. Protecting yourself is not a failure to forgive."],"q":[[24,22,22],[42,40,40],[41,34,34],[3,134,134]],"h":[56],"f":["betrayal_and_broken_trust","conflict_and_reconciliation","anger"],"m":false,"w":["forgiving someone","how do i forgive","should i forgive","letting go of a grudge","i can't forgive them","i cant forgive them","resentment","holding a grudge","العفو","المسامحة","jemandem vergeben","groll","pardonner a quelqu un","pardonner à quelqu'un","rancune","memaafkan orang","dendam","простить человека","обида","affetmek","kin tutmak","کسی کو معاف کرنا","کینہ"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"guarding_the_tongue","k":5,"t":"Guarding Your Tongue","s":"Gossip, backbiting, and words you want back","e":"Most of what a person regrets was said quickly, to someone they trusted, about someone who was not in the room. The Qur’an does not treat that as small. It also does not leave you with only regret: the verse that names backbiting closes by calling Allah Accepting of repentance and Merciful. The Prophet ﷺ gave two options and named the good one first. Speak good, or stay silent. That choice comes back in the next conversation.","a":["Where you spoke against someone, say something true and good about them to the same people.","Ask Allah’s forgiveness now, and take the question of whether to tell the person to someone qualified to answer it."],"q":[[49,12,12],[50,18,18],[17,53,53],[33,70,70],[4,148,148]],"h":[57],"f":["forgiveness_and_repentance","conflict_and_reconciliation","envy_and_jealousy"],"m":false,"w":["slander","i lied","guarding the tongue","watch your tongue","hold my tongue","lying","relying","lying","lies","telling lies","i lie a lot","kaffaratul majlis","dua after a gathering","dua at the end of a gathering","backbiting","backbite","gheebah","gheeba","ghibah","gossip","gossiping","i gossiped","talking behind someone's back","talking behind someones back","i said something bad about someone","something bad","i did something really bad","i said something i regret","namimah","tale carrying","غيبة","نميمة","حفظ اللسان","uble nachrede","üble nachrede","lastern","lästern","medisance","médisance","commerage","commérage","gibah","menggunjing","gosip","сплетни","злословие","gibet","dedikodu","غیبت","چغلی"],"d":[37],"l":"en"},{"id":"betrayal_and_broken_trust","k":5,"t":"Betrayal and Broken Trust","s":"Someone close let you down","e":"Allah commands that trusts be returned to those they belong to, so what happened to you was a real wrong, not an oversensitivity. The Qur’an praises patience and forgiveness as a matter of resolve, and never asks you to hand the same trust back to someone who has not earned it again.","a":["Name to yourself exactly what was broken. Vagueness keeps a wound open longer.","Rebuild trust in steps, if you choose to at all. Trust returns at the speed it is earned."],"q":[[4,58,58],[42,43,43],[16,127,127],[12,86,86]],"h":[42],"f":["forgiving_someone","injustice_and_oppression","heartbreak"],"m":false,"w":["betrayed","betrayal","they betrayed me","backstabbed","broken trust","my friend betrayed me","cheated on me","lied to me","can't trust anyone","خيانة","غدر","verrat","vertrauensbruch","trahison","trahi","dikhianati","pengkhianatan","предательство","предали","ihanet","guven ihaneti","güven ihaneti","دھوکہ","بے وفائی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"children_upbringing","k":5,"t":"Children and Upbringing","s":"Raising children","e":"Luqman’s advice to his son models patient, personal instruction in faith, gratitude, good character and steady worship, given over many gentle conversations rather than one lecture. Allah also tells the Prophet ﷺ to enjoin prayer on his family and to be steadfast in it himself, which puts the example before the instruction.","a":["Have one unhurried conversation with your child today, following Luqman’s gentle example."],"q":[[31,13,19],[66,6,6],[20,132,132]],"h":[],"f":["parents","family_pressure","gratitude"],"m":false,"w":["children","kids","parenting","raising children","my son","my daughter","dua for my baby","dua for baby","dua for a baby","dua for a newborn","dua for newborn","new baby","newborn","parenting advice quran","parenting advice","islamic parenting","quran parenting","raising children in islam","teaching my children","أولاد","تربية الاولاد","kinder","erziehung","enfants","education des enfants","anak","mendidik anak","дети","воспитание","cocuk","çocuk","بچے","اولاد"],"d":[34,38],"l":"en"},{"id":"keeping_family_ties","k":5,"t":"Family Ties","s":"Staying close to relatives","e":"The Qur’an names the ties of kinship beside Allah Himself as something to be mindful of, and warns against severing them. The Prophet ﷺ said that the one who truly keeps ties is not the one who only returns kindness, but the one who reaches out when a relative has cut him off. Keeping ties never means accepting harm: if a relative is hurting you, your safety comes first, and someone qualified can help you weigh what keeping ties asks of you.","a":["Choose one relative you have drifted from and make one small contact this week: a message, a call, or a greeting at the next gathering.","If a relationship is harming you, keep yourself safe first, and ask a person of knowledge what keeping ties asks of you in your situation."],"q":[[4,1,1],[13,21,21],[47,22,23],[16,90,90]],"h":[58,59],"f":["conflict_and_reconciliation","forgiving_someone","parents"],"m":false,"w":["family ties","ties of kinship","kinship","keeping family ties","silat ar rahim","silat al rahim","sila rahim","silah rehmi","silat ul rahim","cutting family ties","cutting off family","cut off my family","cut off by my family","relatives","my relatives","relatives who hurt me","toxic relatives","difficult relatives","siblings","my siblings","brother and sister fighting","fighting with my brother","fighting with my sister","in laws","in-laws","my in laws","problems with in laws","صلة الرحم","قطيعة الرحم","قطع الرحم","الاقارب","verwandtschaft","verwandte","familienbande","liens familiaux","liens de parente","liens de parenté","belle famille","silaturahmi","silaturahim","memutus silaturahmi","родственные связи","родственники","akraba","akrabalik","akrabalık","akrabalarla küs","sila-i rahim","sıla-i rahim","صلہ رحمی","رشتہ داری","رشتہ دار"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"longing_for_a_child","k":5,"t":"Longing for a Child","s":"Waiting and hoping for children","e":"Zakariyya ﷺ asked Allah for a child when his bones had weakened and his hair had turned white, and Ibrahim ﷺ asked to be given a righteous child; the Qur’an records both prayers. It also states that Allah gives daughters to whom He wills and sons to whom He wills, and leaves whom He wills without children. Waiting is not a verdict on your faith or your worth. Keep asking, and seek medical care too: the two do not compete.","a":["Keep asking in your own words as well as in these, and in your prostration too.","See a doctor early, together if you can, and treat their advice as part of your striving rather than a lapse in trust."],"q":[[21,89,90],[19,4,6],[37,100,100],[42,49,50]],"h":[],"f":["delayed_dua","contentment_with_qadr","marital_relationship"],"m":true,"w":["i cant have children","i can't have children","we cant have children","cant conceive","can't conceive","struggling to conceive","trying to conceive","unable to have children","infertility","infertile","childless","no children","waiting for a child","dua to have a child","dua for having children","ivf","can't get pregnant","pregnant\n                // dua","دعاء الانجاب","تاخر الحمل","تأخر الحمل","عدم الانجاب","العقم","kinderwunsch","unfruchtbarkeit","dua fur ein kind","dua für ein kind","desir d enfant","désir d'enfant","infertilite","infertilité","doa minta anak","belum punya anak","belum dikaruniai anak","бесплодие","дуа о ребенке","дуа о ребёнке","не могу забеременеть","cocuk sahibi olmak","çocuk sahibi olmak","cocuk duasi","çocuk duası","kisirlik","kısırlık","اولاد کی دعا","اولاد نہیں","بانجھ پن"],"d":[39],"l":"en"},{"id":"studies_and_exams","k":6,"t":"Studies and Exams","s":"What do I read for an exam?","e":"No verse or recitation guarantees a passing grade, and it would not be a kindness to tell you otherwise. What the sources point to is seeking knowledge sincerely, working consistently, and trusting Allah with the result. Musa ﷺ asked for his chest to be expanded and his task made easy before he faced something hard; you may ask the same.","a":["Study with real, consistent effort. This is the means Allah has placed within your reach.","Make du‘a before and during the exam, then leave the outcome to Allah."],"q":[[20,114,114],[20,25,28],[94,5,6],[3,159,159]],"h":[],"f":["failing_an_exam","anxiety_and_worry","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["dua for memory","dua to remember what i study","improve my memory","exam","exams","test","studying","study","revision","grades","good grades","dua for exam","what do i read for exam","دعاء للامتحان","علم","ilm","prufung","prüfung","klausur","lernen","examen","examens","etudes","études","revisions","révisions","ujian","belajar","doa ujian","экзамен","экзамены","учеба","учёба","sinav","sınav","imtihan","ders calismak","ders çalışmak","امتحان","پڑھائی"],"d":[40,18],"l":"en"},{"id":"failing_an_exam","k":6,"t":"Failing an Exam","s":"The result was not what you hoped","e":"One result is not a verdict on your worth, and it is not a sign that Allah has turned away from you. You may dislike a thing that is good for you; you do not yet see where this route goes. Grieve it for a day, then find the next lawful step and take it.","a":["Find out exactly what went wrong, and treat that as information rather than as identity.","Ask Allah for a good outcome in the matter, then register for the next attempt."],"q":[[2,216,216],[3,139,139],[94,5,6],[65,3,3]],"h":[37],"f":["failure_and_setbacks","feeling_behind_in_life","studies_and_exams"],"m":false,"w":["i failed my exam","failed my exam","failed the test","bad grades","didn't get in","didnt get in","rejected from university","resit","i failed my finals","رسبت في الامتحان","prufung nicht bestanden","prüfung nicht bestanden","durchgefallen","j ai rate mon examen","j'ai raté mon examen","echec examen","gagal ujian","tidak lulus","провалил экзамен","не сдал","sinavi gecemedim","sınavı geçemedim","sinavda kaldim","sınavda kaldım","امتحان میں ناکام"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"seeking_knowledge","k":6,"t":"Seeking Knowledge","s":"Where do I begin learning my deen?","e":"The Qur’an asks whether those who know and those who do not are equal, and the Prophet ﷺ said Allah eases the path to Paradise for whoever walks a path seeking knowledge. Start with what you are obliged to know and act on, and take it from a teacher rather than assembling it alone.","a":["Learn what you are personally obliged to know first: prayer, purification, what you deal in.","Take it from a qualified teacher, consistently, rather than from scattered clips."],"q":[[39,9,9],[20,114,114],[35,28,28],[29,69,69]],"h":[],"f":["studies_and_exams","doubts_and_waswas","weak_faith_returning_to_allah"],"m":false,"w":["seeking knowledge","learning islam","where do i start learning","how do i learn my deen","studying islam","islamic knowledge","طلب العلم","تعلم الدين","wissen suchen","islam lernen","quete du savoir","quête du savoir","apprendre l islam","menuntut ilmu","belajar agama","поиск знаний","изучать ислам","ilim ogrenmek","ilim öğrenmek","dini ogrenmek","dini öğrenmek","علم حاصل کرنا","دین سیکھنا"],"d":[40],"l":"en"},{"id":"asking_a_person_of_knowledge","k":6,"t":"Asking Someone Who Knows","s":"Taking a real question to a scholar","e":"Some questions have an answer, and it lives with a person rather than in an app. Whether a thing is permitted for you, what your ablution requires, how many units a particular prayer has in your school: these are rulings. They turn on details of your own situation. The Qur’an’s instruction for not knowing is to ask the people of knowledge. That is not a dismissal: it is faster than searching, and the answer will actually fit your circumstances rather than somebody else’s.","a":["Ask a qualified scholar or imam who can hear your actual situation, rather than searching for someone else’s answer.","Give them the whole picture, including the part you would rather leave out. A ruling on half the facts answers a different question."],"q":[[16,43,43],[21,7,7],[20,114,114]],"h":[20],"f":["seeking_knowledge","doubts_and_waswas","new_to_islam"],"m":false,"w":["ask a scholar","ask an imam","ask a shaykh","ask a sheikh","ask a person of knowledge","who do i ask","where do i ask","fatwa","fatwah","ruling","islamic ruling","what is the ruling","is this halal","is this haram","is it halal","is it haram","halal or haram","permissible","is it permissible","fiqh","fiqh question","madhhab","mazhab","school of thought","wudu","ablution","abdest","الوضوء","broke my wudu","can i pray without wudu","what breaks wudu","does this break my wudu","ghusl","tayammum","purity","menstruation and prayer","period and prayer","period and fasting","how many rakat","how many rakah","sunnah prayers","nafl prayer","witr","qasr prayer","combining prayers","i broke my fast","broke","i broke my fast","broke my fast","missed fasts","make up missed fasts","qada fasts","kaffarah","fidya","is music haram","mixed gender","insurance halal","mortgage halal","أسأل عالما","فتوى","حكم","هل هذا حلال","هل هذا حرام","نواقض الوضوء","gelehrten fragen","fatwa","ist das halal","ist das haram","demander a un savant","fatwa","est ce halal","est ce haram","tanya ustadz","tanya ulama","fatwa","apakah halal","apakah haram","спросить учёного","фетва","это халяль","это харам","alime sormak","fetva","helal mi","haram mi","abdesti bozan","عالم سے پوچھیں","فتویٰ","کیا یہ حلال ہے","کیا یہ حرام ہے","وضو ٹوٹنا"],"d":[40],"l":"en"},{"id":"work_provision_and_debt","k":6,"t":"Money and Provision","s":"Money worries","e":"Provision is described as coming from Allah through means He opens, an invitation to lawful effort together with trust, not a promise that money never runs short. Musa ﷺ asked plainly for whatever good Allah would send him, at a moment when he had nothing. That is a du‘a you are allowed to make.","a":["Take every lawful, practical step available to you, and pair it with sincere du‘a.","Write down what actually comes in and goes out this month. Uncertainty makes fear larger than the numbers."],"q":[[65,2,3],[11,6,6],[28,24,24],[51,22,22]],"h":[37],"f":["debt","losing_work","halal_provision"],"m":false,"w":["money","money worries","money stress","provision","rizq","rizk","financial difficulty","can't afford","cant afford","broke","no money","bills","poverty","رزق","ضيق مالي","geldsorgen","finanzielle probleme","problemes d argent","problèmes d'argent","soucis financiers","masalah keuangan","rezeki","tidak punya uang","нет денег","финансовые проблемы","para sikintisi","para sıkıntısı","rizik","پیسوں کی پریشانی","رزق"],"d":[1],"l":"en"},{"id":"debt","k":6,"t":"Debt","s":"Owing more than you can repay","e":"Debt is treated seriously in the sources and never as a moral collapse. The Qur’an instructs the creditor to grant time if the debtor is in hardship, and the Prophet ﷺ sought refuge in Allah from the burden of debt by name, which tells you the weight you are feeling is recognised.","a":["Write the full amount down and make a repayment plan, however slow. A named number is smaller than a feared one.","Speak to whoever you owe before the date, not after it. Honesty preserves more than money."],"q":[[2,280,280],[65,7,7],[65,2,3],[2,275,275]],"h":[29],"f":["work_provision_and_debt","anxiety_and_worry","halal_provision"],"m":false,"w":["debt","in debt","i owe money","loan","loans","credit card debt","can't pay back","cant pay back","riba","interest","دين","ديون","schulden","kredit","dette","dettes","endette","endetté","hutang","utang","berhutang","долг","долги","кредит","borc","borç","kredi","قرض","ادھار"],"d":[1,41,42],"l":"en"},{"id":"losing_work","k":6,"t":"Losing Work","s":"Out of work, and worried","e":"Losing work costs more than income; it takes a place in the day and a sense of being needed. Musa ﷺ, with nothing and nowhere to go, said simply that he was in need of whatever good Allah sent him, and what came next was work, and a household. Ask, then apply.","a":["Keep a shape to the day while you look: a fixed waking time, and the prayers on time.","Tell people you trust that you are looking. Most work is found through someone, not through a form."],"q":[[65,2,3],[28,24,24],[94,5,6],[11,6,6]],"h":[37],"f":["work_provision_and_debt","failure_and_setbacks","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["lost my job","made redundant","laid off","fired","unemployed","no job","looking for a job","looking for work","job search","job interview","dua for a job","dua for job","dua for work","career","دعاء للعمل","ابحث عن عمل","jobsuche","recherche d emploi","recherche d'emploi","mencari kerja","doa mencari kerja","поиск работы","is arama","iş arama","نوکری کی دعا","out of work","job hunting","can't find work","cant find work","فقدت عملي","بلا عمل","job verloren","arbeitslos","gekundigt","gekündigt","perdu mon emploi","au chomage","au chômage","licencie","licencié","kehilangan pekerjaan","menganggur","di phk","потерял работу","безработный","isimi kaybettim","işimi kaybettim","issiz","işsiz","نوکری چلی گئی","بے روزگار"],"d":[1,18],"l":"en"},{"id":"halal_provision","k":6,"t":"Halal Provision","s":"Is what I earn permissible?","e":"The Qur’an tells people to eat of what is lawful and good on the earth, and draws a clear line between trade and interest. A specific job, contract or product is a ruling. Take it to a qualified scholar rather than settling it from a search result, and do not assume the worst about yourself before you have asked.","a":["Write down the exact part you are unsure about, and ask a qualified scholar about that part.","If a change is needed, plan it in steps. Leaving something for Allah rarely happens in one day."],"q":[[2,168,168],[2,275,275],[65,2,3],[11,6,6]],"h":[60],"f":["work_provision_and_debt","debt","tawakkul_trust_in_allah"],"m":false,"w":["halal income","halal provision","is my job halal","haram money","business","my business","starting a business","haram job","working in a bank","halal earnings","halal rizq","رزق حلال","كسب حلال","halal einkommen","haram geld","revenu halal","argent haram","rezeki halal","penghasilan halal","uang haram","халяльный заработок","харам деньги","helal kazanc","helal kazanç","haram para","حلال رزق","حرام کمائی"],"d":[41],"l":"en"},{"id":"feeling_behind_in_life","k":6,"t":"Feeling Behind in Life","s":"Everyone else seems further along","e":"Allah tells the Prophet ﷺ not to strain his eyes toward what others have been given. The comparison itself is named as the harm. Ad-Duha was revealed to somebody who looked, from outside, as though everything had stopped. Timelines are not the measure; taqwa is, and yours is still open.","a":["Mute what you are comparing yourself against for a week, and see what is left.","Pick one thing that is genuinely yours to move, and move it this week."],"q":[[93,3,5],[20,131,131],[2,216,216],[65,3,3]],"h":[37],"f":["envy_and_jealousy","contentment_with_qadr","low_self_worth"],"m":false,"w":["behind in life","everyone is ahead of me","falling behind","wasted my twenties","too late for me","life is passing me by","everyone else has it together","still nothing at my age","متاخر في حياتي","im leben zuruck","im leben zurück","abgehangt","abgehängt","en retard dans la vie","je stagne","tertinggal","ketinggalan dari yang lain","отстаю от жизни","все обогнали","hayatta geri kaldim","hayatta geri kaldım","زندگی میں پیچھے"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"decision_making_istikhara","k":7,"t":"A Difficult Decision (Istikharah)","s":"Making a hard decision","e":"Istikharah is exactly what its name means: asking the One who knows what you do not, then acting with a settled heart whichever way things unfold. It is not a dream and not a sign to wait for. The Qur’an pairs consultation and decision with reliance on Allah, in that order.","a":["Pray two units of voluntary prayer, then say the istikharah supplication below.","Take ordinary, sensible steps too: ask people whose judgement you trust. Istikharah supports good effort rather than replacing it."],"q":[[3,159,159],[2,216,216],[65,3,3]],"h":[61],"f":["tawakkul_trust_in_allah","fear_of_the_future","contentment_with_qadr"],"m":false,"w":["istikhara","istikharah","hard decision","difficult decision","which choice","istikhara dua","salat al istikhara","how to pray istikhara","career decision","career choice","which job should i take","دعاء الاستخارة","صلاة الاستخارة","doa istikharah","sholat istikharah","дуа истихара","istihare","istihare duasi","istihare duası","استخارہ کی دعا","should i","how much quran should i read","should i\n                // move house","should i take this job\n                // istikhara","istikhara","i don't know what to choose","i dont know what to choose","i don't know what to do","i dont know what to do","help me decide","cant decide","can't decide","which one should i choose","big decision","istikhara dream","dream after istikhara","do i need a dream for istikhara","استخارة","schwere entscheidung","decision difficile","décision difficile","keputusan sulit","istikharah","трудное решение","istihare","zor karar","استخارہ","مشکل فیصلہ"],"d":[43],"l":"en"},{"id":"tawakkul_trust_in_allah","k":7,"t":"Tawakkul (Trust in Allah)","s":"You have done your part","e":"Tawakkul is trust after effort, not instead of it. The Qur’an pairs relying on Allah with having first decided and taken the steps in your control, and the Prophet ﷺ instructed being keen on what benefits you and seeking Allah’s help in the same breath. Do your part, then genuinely hand the rest over.","a":["Do what is within your control, then consciously hand the rest to Allah rather than continuing to carry it.","When “if only” starts, stop the sentence. The Prophet ﷺ named it as a door best left shut."],"q":[[3,159,159],[65,3,3],[3,173,173],[9,51,51]],"h":[37,3],"f":["contentment_with_qadr","fear_of_the_future","decision_making_istikhara"],"m":false,"w":["tawakkul","trust in allah","trusting allah","relying on allah","reliance on allah","letting go and trusting allah","i did my part","توكل","التوكل على الله","gottvertrauen","confiance en allah","tawakal","berserah diri","упование на аллаха","tevekkul","tevekkül","توکل","اللہ پر بھروسہ"],"d":[22],"l":"en"},{"id":"dunya_is_temporary","k":7,"t":"This World Is Temporary","s":"Putting the dunya in its place","e":"The Qur’an calls the life of this world an enjoyment of delusion, and likens it to rain that greens the earth and then dries. Read that in your own translation rather than in a slogan: it is not contempt for the world, but an accurate measure of it against what lasts.","a":["Give something away this week: money, time, or an hour of your attention.","Ask which of the things worrying you today will matter in ten years, and act accordingly."],"q":[[57,20,20],[18,45,46],[87,16,17],[102,1,2],[3,185,185],[63,9,9]],"h":[62],"f":["preparing_for_the_akhirah","envy_and_jealousy","feeling_behind_in_life"],"m":false,"w":["dunya","this world is temporary","dunya is temporary","chasing the dunya","attached to the dunya","material things","what is the point of all this","الدنيا","الدنيا فانية","diesseits","verganglich","vergänglich","bas monde","bas-monde","ephemere","éphémère","dunia sementara","dunia fana","мирская жизнь","бренность","dunya gecici","dünya geçici","دنیا فانی","دنیا عارضی"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"preparing_for_the_akhirah","k":7,"t":"Preparing for the Akhirah","s":"What am I sending ahead?","e":"The Qur’an asks every soul to look at what it has sent ahead for tomorrow, and says an atom’s weight of good will be seen. That is a small enough measure to start with today. The Prophet ﷺ warned against overwhelming yourself, so build something steady rather than something impressive.","a":["Choose one deed you will do every day, and keep it even on the days it feels pointless.","Settle one thing you would not want to leave unsettled: a debt, an apology, a will."],"q":[[59,18,18],[99,7,8],[3,185,185],[87,16,17],[103,1,3]],"h":[1],"f":["dunya_is_temporary","bereavement_and_death","laziness_and_discipline"],"m":false,"w":["akhirah","hereafter","afterlife","preparing for death","day of judgement","what happens after we die","am i ready to die","grave","jannah","dying","doing","scared of dying","afraid of dying","scared of death","afraid of death","fear of death","i dont want to die","hell","hello","Ehe","الاخرة","يوم القيامة","jenseits","jungster tag","jüngster tag","au dela","au-delà","jour du jugement","akhirat","hari kiamat","bekal akhirat","загробная жизнь","судный день","ahiret","kiyamet","kıyamet","آخرت","قیامت"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"dreams_and_their_place","k":8,"t":"Dreams, and What They Are","s":"A dream, and what to do with it","e":"The Sunnah does not treat every dream as a message. What is reported is three kinds: glad tidings from Allah, a distressing one from Shaytan, and what your own mind was already turning over. That third kind is the reason a dream is not, by itself, information about your life. If yours was good, thank Allah and tell someone who will be glad for you. If it disturbed you, there is guidance for that too, and none of it involves working out what it meant.","a":["If the dream was good, thank Allah for it, and tell only someone you trust to be glad for you.","Do not act on a dream. Nothing reported makes a dream a reason to decide anything."],"q":[[30,23,23],[39,42,42]],"h":[63,64],"f":["frightening_dreams","dream_interpretation","is_this_a_sign"],"m":false,"w":["dream","dreams","i had a dream","i had a good dream","good dream","nice dream","i keep dreaming","should i tell people my dream","who can i tell my dream to","telling someone my dream","dreams in islam","ruya","rooya","رؤيا","حلم","الرؤيا في الاسلام","المنام","traum","traume","träume","guter traum","reve","rêve","rêves","beau reve","mimpi","mimpi baik","mimpi dalam islam","сон","сны","хороший сон","ruya","rüya","guzel ruya","rüyalar","خواب","اچھا خواب","خواب اسلام میں"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"frightening_dreams","k":8,"t":"A Frightening Dream","s":"Nightmares, and waking afraid","e":"Waking with your heart going and the dream still in the room is frightening, and it is not a sign that something is wrong with your faith. Abu Salamah, one of the Companions, said that he used to be so shaken by dreams that he would tremble, until he was taught what to do about them. What is reported ends by saying that it will not harm you. And if they come night after night and your sleep is going, that is worth telling a doctor as well; the two are not in competition.","a":["Seek refuge in Allah from it, and do not tell people about it. Both are what is reported.","Get up and pray, even briefly. It is the reported response, and it also breaks the loop of lying there.","If frightening dreams are nightly and your sleep is suffering, speak to a doctor too. That is not a lack of trust in Allah."],"q":[[113,1,5],[2,255,255],[13,28,28]],"h":[64,63],"f":["dreams_and_their_place","protection_from_whispers","before_sleeping"],"m":true,"w":["nightmare","nightmares","bad dream","bad dreams","scary dream","frightening dream","terrifying dream","keep having bad dreams","i wake up terrified","i wake up scared","cant sleep because of dreams","night terrors","disturbing dreams","recurring nightmare","كابوس","احلام مزعجة","حلم مخيف","albtraum","albtraume","albträume","schlechter traum","cauchemar","cauchemars","mauvais reve","mimpi buruk","mimpi menakutkan","кошмар","кошмары","плохой сон","kotu ruya","kötü rüya","kabus","برا خواب","ڈراؤنا خواب"],"d":[0],"l":"en"},{"id":"dream_interpretation","k":8,"t":"What a Dream Meant","s":"Why a dream is not read here","e":"Interpretation is a real knowledge, which the Qur’an describes as something Allah taught Yusuf, and it is not a list of symbols. In that same account, a king’s own court is asked to interpret a dream and answers plainly that they are not learned in it. The confident meanings you can find in a minute of searching are a dictionary somebody invented. What is reported is that a dream should be told only to someone with knowledge, or someone who will give you sincere counsel.","a":["If it troubles you, take it to a person of knowledge who knows you, not to a stranger, and not to a website.","Do not change a decision about marriage, work, money or your religion because of a dream."],"q":[[12,6,6],[12,44,44],[12,101,101]],"h":[65],"f":["asking_a_person_of_knowledge","dreams_and_their_place","is_this_a_sign"],"m":false,"w":["dream","dreams","dream interpretation","dream meaning","meaning of dreams","meaning of my dream","what does my dream mean","what do dreams mean","interpret my dream","tell me what my dream means","can you interpret my dream","dream dictionary","tabir","tabeer","ta'wil","tawil","i saw the prophet in a dream","i saw someone who died in a dream","someone","died","someone close to\n                // me died","تفسير الاحلام","تعبير الرؤيا","تأويل الاحلام","ماذا يعني حلمي","traumdeutung","was bedeutet mein traum","interpretation des reves","signification des reves","tafsir mimpi","arti mimpi","makna mimpi","толкование снов","что означает мой сон","ruya tabiri","rüya tabiri","ruyamin anlami","خواب کی تعبیر","خواب کا مطلب"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"is_this_a_sign","k":8,"t":"Is This a Sign?","s":"Waiting for a sign from Allah","e":"Waiting for a sign is often a way of postponing a decision you already have to make, and it can go on for years. The Qur’an names the unseen as Allah’s alone; nobody is given a reading of it, and a coincidence is not a message you have been sent. The supplication that teaches istikharah asks for the matter to be decreed if it is good and turned away if it is harmful, and then asks to be made content with it. It names no dream and no sign to wait for. You are allowed to take advice, weigh it, choose, and trust.","a":["Name the decision, take advice from someone whose judgement you trust, and give yourself a date to choose by.","Make istikharah, then act on the better option as you see it. A settled heart afterwards is not the same thing as a sign beforehand."],"q":[[27,65,65],[31,34,34],[2,216,216],[65,3,3]],"h":[61],"f":["decision_making_istikhara","tawakkul_trust_in_allah","dream_interpretation"],"m":false,"w":["sign from allah","a sign from allah","is this a sign","was that a sign","is allah showing me something","allah is showing me something","is this a message from allah","signs from allah","i keep seeing the same thing","istikhara dream","dream after istikhara","sign after istikhara","do i need a dream for istikhara","no dream after istikhara","coincidence or sign","how do i know allah wants this","علامة من الله","هل هذه علامة","استخارة وحلم","zeichen von allah","ist das ein zeichen","signe d allah","est ce un signe","tanda dari allah","apakah ini tanda","petunjuk allah","знак от аллаха","это знак","allahtan bir isaret","bu bir isaret mi","اللہ کی طرف سے نشانی","کیا یہ نشانی ہے"],"d":[],"l":"en"},{"id":"before_sleeping","k":9,"t":"Before Sleeping","s":"What should I read before sleep?","e":"A short, well attested set of recitations before sleep is part of the Prophetic practice: Ayat al-Kursi, and the three short surahs at the end of the Qur’an, read in your own selected translation and script.","a":["Recite these before sleeping tonight, in your own time. Open each one directly in the reader.","If sleeplessness goes on for weeks, speak to a doctor as well as making du‘a."],"q":[[2,255,255],[112,1,4],[113,1,5],[114,1,6]],"h":[66],"f":["morning_and_evening_remembrance","seeking_protection","night_prayer"],"m":false,"w":["before sleeping","before sleep","before bed","what to read before sleep","sleep dua","bedtime dua","ayat al kursi before sleep","can't sleep","i cant sleep","cant sleep","insomnia","trouble sleeping","dua before sleeping","bismika allahumma amutu wa ahya","نوم","قبل النوم","vor dem schlafen","vorm schlafengehen","avant de dormir","avant le coucher","sebelum tidur","doa tidur","перед сном","uyumadan once","uyumadan önce","uyku duasi","uyku duası","سونے سے پہلے","نیند کی دعا"],"d":[44,45,15],"l":"en"},{"id":"morning_and_evening_remembrance","k":9,"t":"Morning and Evening Remembrance","s":"Daily adhkar","e":"Short, regular remembrance in the morning and evening is a widely known Prophetic practice, built around Ayat al-Kursi and the three short surahs. It is a steady habit rather than something done once. A minute after Fajr and a minute after Asr is enough to begin.","a":["Set aside a minute after Fajr and after Asr for these, and open each verse directly in the reader."],"q":[[2,255,255],[112,1,4],[113,1,5],[114,1,6],[13,28,28]],"h":[],"f":["before_sleeping","seeking_protection","anxiety_and_worry"],"m":false,"w":["morning adhkar","evening adhkar","azkar","adhkar","morning remembrance","evening remembrance","daily dhikr","أذكار الصباح","أذكار المساء","morning dua","evening dua","morning duas","dua in the morning","adhkar al sabah","adhkar al masa","azkar e subah","morgengedenken","abendgedenken","invocations du matin","adhkar du matin","dzikir pagi","dzikir petang","dzikir pagi petang","утренние азкары","вечерние азкары","sabah zikirleri","aksam zikirleri","akşam zikirleri","صبح شام کے اذکار"],"d":[46,47,16],"l":"en"},{"id":"seeking_protection","k":9,"t":"Seeking Protection","s":"Protection for yourself and your home","e":"The Qur’an closes with two surahs that are themselves the seeking of refuge. The harm named in them includes envy and whispering, which is to say ordinary human harms. Keep to what is authentically reported and do not go looking for practices nobody can source for you.","a":["Read the last two surahs and Ayat al-Kursi as a settled daily habit, morning and evening.","If you are afraid of harm from a person, take practical protective steps as well as reciting."],"q":[[113,1,5],[114,1,6],[2,255,255],[16,98,98]],"h":[66],"f":["protection_from_whispers","morning_and_evening_remembrance","envy_and_jealousy"],"m":false,"w":["protection","protect me","evil eye","nazar","ruqyah","black magic","sihr","protection for my family","protection for my home","seeking refuge","muawwidhatayn","الحماية","العين","الرقية","schutz","boser blick","böser blick","protection","mauvais oeil","mauvais œil","ain","pain","dua for rain","again","explain","perlindungan","penyakit ain","terkena ain","ruqyah","защита","сглаз","korunma","nazar","حفاظت","نظر بد"],"d":[22,48,47],"l":"en"},{"id":"travel_dua","k":9,"t":"Travel","s":"Du‘a for travelling","e":"The Qur’an records a short du‘a for setting out on a journey, recognising that safe travel is something we are given rather than something we control outright.","a":["Say the du‘a for setting out as you leave, and the words for stopping somewhere when you arrive.","For shortening or combining prayers while travelling, ask a person of knowledge; the schools of law differ in the details."],"q":[[43,13,14]],"h":[],"f":["tawakkul_trust_in_allah","seeking_protection","asking_a_person_of_knowledge"],"m":false,"w":["travel","traveling","travelling","journey dua","dua for travel","safar","flight","سفر","journey","going on a trip","safe journey","dua for safe journey","travel dua","dua for travelling","safar dua","dua when boarding plane","flight dua","dua in the car","coming home","returning from travel","dua when arriving","subhanalladhi sakhkhara lana","دعاء السفر","السفر","reise","reisen","preisen","preise","reisegebet","auf reisen","eine reise","dua fur die reise","dua für die reise","dua du voyage","invocation du voyage","voyage","voyager","doa perjalanan","doa naik kendaraan","doa bepergian","perjalanan","дуа в путешествии","дуа путника","путешествие","поездка","yolculuk duasi","yolculuk duası","yolculuk","seyahat","sefer duasi","sefer duası","سفر کی دعا"],"d":[49,50,51],"l":"en"},{"id":"everyday_duas","k":9,"t":"Everyday Du‘as","s":"Eating, going out, the mosque","e":"Remembrance is not kept for the prayer mat. The Qur’an describes people who remember Allah standing, sitting and lying on their sides, and the Sunnah gives short words for ordinary moments: before and after eating, on leaving the house, on entering the mosque. Each of them takes only a moment.","a":["Pick one moment you pass through every day, such as going out of the door, and learn its words this week.","Say Allah’s name before you eat. It is the simplest of these, and the one the Prophet ﷺ taught a boy in his care."],"q":[[33,41,42],[3,191,191]],"h":[67,68],"f":["morning_and_evening_remembrance","before_sleeping","wudu_and_purity"],"m":false,"w":["everyday duas","everyday dua","daily duas","duas for every day","dua before eating","dua before food","what to say before eating","bismillah before eating","bismillah before food","dua after eating","dua after food","dua after a meal","dua when leaving the house","dua leaving home","dua for leaving home","dua when going out","dua entering the mosque","dua for entering the masjid","dua entering masjid","entering the mosque","going to the mosque","how to do dhikr","remembering allah","remember allah","dhikr through the day","subhanallah","subhanallahi wa bihamdihi","دعاء الطعام","دعاء قبل الاكل","دعاء بعد الاكل","دعاء الخروج من المنزل","دعاء دخول المسجد","ذكر الله","dua vor dem essen","dua nach dem essen","dua beim verlassen des hauses","dua beim betreten der moschee","dua avant de manger","invocation avant de manger","dua apres le repas","dua après le repas","invocation en sortant de la maison","en entrant a la mosquee","en entrant à la mosquée","doa makan","doa sebelum makan","doa sesudah makan","doa keluar rumah","doa masuk masjid","дуа перед едой","дуа после еды","молитва перед едой","дуа при выходе из дома","дуа при входе в мечеть","yemek duasi","yemek duası","evden cikarken dua","evden çıkarken dua","camiye girerken dua","camiye girerken okunan dua","کھانے کی دعا","کھانے سے پہلے کی دعا","گھر سے نکلنے کی دعا","مسجد میں داخل ہونے کی دعا"],"d":[48,52,53,54],"l":"en"}],"cites":[{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"684c","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:684c","g":"Sahih","n":"Anas ibn Malik","s":"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it should pray it when he remembers. The narration names no other penance.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"39","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:39","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said this religion is ease, and that whoever overburdens himself in it will be overcome by it, so be balanced, keep close to what is right, and take from acts of worship what you can sustain.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"527","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:527","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah","s":"Asked which deed is most beloved to Allah, the Prophet ﷺ named first the prayer offered at its time.","l":"en"},{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"2516","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:2516","g":"Hasan Sahih (per at-Tirmidhi)","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ told Ibn ‘Abbas to be mindful of Allah and he would find Allah before him; and that when he asks, he should ask of Allah, and when he seeks help, he should seek it from Allah.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2735a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2735a","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that a servant’s supplication continues to be answered as long as he does not grow impatient and say, “I supplicated and I was not answered.”","l":"en"},{"c":"Mishkat al-Masabih","r":"2175","u":"https://sunnah.com/mishkat:2175","g":"Hasan (per al-Albani)","n":null,"s":"Reciting Surah al-Kahf on Friday is reported as a light between the two Fridays. Transmitted by al-Bayhaqi rather than by either Sahih, and graded hasan.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"1047","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:1047","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)","n":null,"s":"Sending salawat upon the Prophet ﷺ is emphasised on Friday.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"38","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:38","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and in hope of its reward will have their past sins forgiven.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"2024","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:2024","g":"Sahih","n":"'Aishah","s":"In the last ten nights the Prophet ﷺ increased his worship, kept the night in prayer, and woke his family for it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"2017","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:2017","g":"Sahih","n":"'Aishah","s":"Laylat al-Qadr is sought in the odd nights of the last ten of Ramadan.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"482","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:482","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the nearest a servant comes to his Lord is while prostrating, and instructed supplicating much in that state.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1229","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1229","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ ended a prayer after two units. When Dhul-Yadayn told him he had forgotten, he prayed the remaining two, gave the closing salutation, and then made two prostrations.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1142","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1142","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ described Shaytan tying three knots on a sleeper, each undone in turn when the person remembers Allah, then performs ablution, then prays, and said that such a person rises in good spirits.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"597a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:597a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that whoever, after every prayer, glorifies Allah 33 times, praises Him 33 times and magnifies Him 33 times, then completes a hundred by declaring that there is no god but Allah alone, will have their wrongs forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"844","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:844","g":"Sahih","n":"Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah","s":"Al-Mughirah ibn Shu‘bah wrote that after every obligatory prayer the Prophet ﷺ would declare that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, His the dominion and His the praise, and that none can withhold what Allah gives or give what He withholds.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"223","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:223","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Malik al-Ash'ari","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that purification is half of faith, and that prayer is a light.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"244","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:244","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that when a believer washes his face, his hands and his feet in wudu, the wrongs done with them leave with the water, until he comes out cleansed of sin.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6464","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6464","g":"Sahih","n":"'Aishah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the deed most beloved to Allah is the most constant one, even if it is little.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"804a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:804a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Umamah al-Bahili","s":"The Prophet ﷺ instructed reciting the Qur’an, saying that it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for its people.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5027","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5027","g":"Sahih","n":"'Uthman ibn 'Affan","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the best of you are those who learn the Qur’an and teach it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"71","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:71","g":"Sahih","n":"Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that when Allah wills good for a person, He gives him understanding of the religion, and that he himself only distributes while Allah is the One who gives.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"4937","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:4937","g":"Sahih","n":"'Aishah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ described one who recites the Qur’an having memorised it as being with the noble scribes, and said that one who keeps at it while it remains hard for him has two rewards.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"791","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:791","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari","s":"The Prophet ﷺ instructed keeping a firm hold on the Qur’an, and swore that it slips away more readily than tethered camels.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5050","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5050","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud","s":"The Prophet ﷺ asked Ibn Mas‘ud to recite to him. When he reached a verse of Surat an-Nisa he was told that was enough, and looked up to find the Prophet’s ﷺ eyes overflowing with tears.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1067","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1067","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud","s":"Ibn Mas‘ud reported that the Prophet ﷺ recited Surat an-Najm and prostrated during it, and that those with him prostrated too.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"578a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:578a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah","s":"Abu Hurayrah prostrated on reciting Surat al-Inshiqaq, and afterwards told those present that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prostrated at it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1077","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1077","g":"Sahih","n":"Rabi'ah ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab","s":"A Companion report: reciting Surat an-Nahl from the pulpit, ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab said that whoever prostrates has done right and that there is no sin upon one who does not, and did not prostrate that day. Ibn ‘Umar added that the prostration of recitation was not made obligatory.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1423","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1423","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Among the seven Allah shades on a day when there is no shade but His is a person who gives in charity so quietly that one hand does not know what the other gave.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2999","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2999","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said the believer’s situation is remarkable: all of it is good for them. If ease comes and they are grateful, that is good for them; and if hardship comes and they endure it patiently, that too is good for them.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6363","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6363","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge in Allah from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, from the burden of debt and from being overpowered by others.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"1319","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:1319","g":"Hasan (per al-Albani)","n":null,"s":"It is reported that when something distressed the Prophet ﷺ, he would turn to prayer. No number of units is named in the narration.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6114","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6114","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the strong person is not the one who overcomes others, but the one who controls himself when he is angry.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2564c","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2564c","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Allah does not look at your faces or your wealth. He looks at your hearts and your deeds.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6306","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6306","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ taught a particular supplication for seeking forgiveness and called it the finest way of asking Allah to forgive.","l":"en"},{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"2398","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:2398","g":"Hasan sahih (per at-Tirmidhi); Hasan (per Ali Zai)","n":"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas","s":"Asked which people are tested most severely, the Prophet ﷺ answered: the prophets, then those nearest to them, then those nearest to them. A person is tried according to their religion, and the trial does not leave them until they walk the earth with no sin upon them.","l":"en"},{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"2396","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:2396","g":"Hasan (per al-Albani)","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the greater the reward, the greater the trial; that when Allah loves a people He tests them; and that whoever is content has Allah’s pleasure, while whoever is angry has His displeasure.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5641","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5641","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that no fatigue, illness, worry, grief, hurt or distress reaches a Muslim, even the prick of a thorn, without Allah expiating some of their wrongs by it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2664","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2664","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said to be keen on what benefits you, to seek Allah’s help and not to give up; and if something goes against you, not to say “if only I had done otherwise”, but to say that Allah decreed it and did what He willed.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5678","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5678","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that Allah has not sent down any disease without also sending down its cure.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1283","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1283","g":"Sahih","n":"Anas ibn Malik","s":"The Prophet ﷺ passed a woman weeping at a grave and told her to fear Allah and be patient. Not knowing who he was, she told him to leave, since he had not been struck by what struck her. When she learned who he was she came to his door, and he said that patience is at the first stroke.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"918a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:918a","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ taught that whoever is struck by a calamity should say the words the Qur’an teaches, and then ask Allah to reward them in their affliction and give them something better in its place.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"1631","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:1631","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that when a person dies their deeds come to an end except for three: ongoing charity, knowledge that others benefit from, and a righteous child who prays for them.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2577a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2577a","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"In a narration from the Prophet ﷺ, Allah says that He has forbidden injustice for Himself and made it forbidden among His servants, so they must not wrong one another.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1496","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1496","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas","s":"Sending Mu‘adh to Yemen, the Prophet ﷺ warned him to beware the supplication of the wronged, because there is no veil between it and Allah.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"202","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:202","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As","s":"The Prophet ﷺ recited the words of Ibrahim and of ‘Isa about their peoples, then raised his hands and said “O Allah, my Ummah, my Ummah”, and wept. Allah sent Jibril to ask him why he wept, and answered that He would please him concerning his Ummah and would not displease him.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"249a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:249a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"At a graveyard the Prophet ﷺ greeted its people and said he wished he could see our brothers. The Companions asked whether they were not his brothers. He answered that they are his companions, and that our brothers are the ones who have not yet come.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"199a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:199a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that every prophet was given one supplication that is answered, and that each of them hastened to use it. He said he had withheld his own and kept it as intercession for his Ummah on the Day of Resurrection, for whoever of them dies without associating anything with Allah.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"349","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:349","g":"Sahih","n":"Anas ibn Malik","s":"On the night journey fifty prayers were enjoined. Each time the Prophet ﷺ passed Musa, Musa told him his Ummah would not be able to bear it and urged him to ask his Lord for relief. Allah reduced them until they were five, and said that they are five and they are fifty, for His Word does not change.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"887","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:887","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that were it not that he would make it hard for his Ummah, he would have told them to use the siwak before every prayer.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2747a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2747a","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ described Allah’s joy at a servant’s repentance as greater than a traveller’s joy at unexpectedly finding a lost mount in the desert.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"7507","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:7507","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"In a narration of the Prophet ﷺ, a servant sins and asks forgiveness, then sins again and asks again, and each time Allah says that His servant knows he has a Lord who forgives sins and takes him to account, and forgives him.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6000","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6000","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Allah made mercy a hundred parts. He kept all but one of them with Him and sent that one part down, and it is by that single part that every creature shows mercy to another.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"7405","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:7405","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Allah says that He is as His servant thinks of Him, and that He is with him when he remembers Him. Whoever comes toward Him walking, He comes toward running.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"121","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:121","g":"Sahih","n":"Ibn Shamasah al-Mahri, from 'Amr ibn al-'As","s":"‘Amr ibn al-‘As recalled asking the Prophet ﷺ to pardon him as a condition of accepting Islam, and being asked in reply whether he did not know that Islam wipes out what came before it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5971","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5971","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Asked who most deserves his good companionship, the Prophet ﷺ answered: your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6077","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6077","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari","s":"It is not lawful for a Muslim to cut himself off from his brother beyond three nights, each turning away when they meet. The better of the two is the one who greets first.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2588","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2588","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that charity does not decrease wealth, that Allah only increases a servant in honour for pardoning, and that no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6018","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6018","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or stay silent. It was said together with not harming a neighbour and honouring a guest.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5991","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5991","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn 'Amr","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the one who keeps the ties of kinship is not the one who only repays what he is given, but the one who restores the tie when it has been cut.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2558a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2558a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"A man told the Prophet ﷺ that he kept ties with relatives who cut him off, was good to them while they wronged him, and was patient while they were harsh. He was told that if it was as he said, it was as though he were feeding them hot ashes, and that a helper from Allah would stay with him against them as long as he kept to it.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"2072","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:2072","g":"Sahih","n":"al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib","s":"Nobody has eaten better food than what he eats from the work of his own hand, and the prophet Dawud عليه السلام ate from the work of his hand.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1166","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1166","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ taught his companions a specific prayer and supplication for seeking Allah’s guidance before a decision.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6416","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6416","g":"Sahih","n":"'Abdullah ibn 'Umar","s":"The Prophet ﷺ took Ibn ‘Umar by the shoulder and told him to be in this world as a stranger, or as someone crossing a road.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2263a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2263a","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ described dreams as being of three kinds: glad tidings from Allah, a distressing one from Shaytan, and what a person’s own mind was turning over. He instructed one who sees what he dislikes to get up and pray, and not to relate it to people.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6986","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6986","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Qatadah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that a good dream is from Allah and a distressing one from Shaytan, and instructed one who sees a dream he dislikes to seek refuge in Allah from Shaytan and turn aside, saying that it will not harm him.","l":"en"},{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"2280","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:2280","g":"Hasan Sahih (per at-Tirmidhi); Sahih (per Darussalam)","n":"Abu Hurayrah","s":"The Prophet ﷺ described dreams as being of three kinds, and said that a dream is not to be related except to someone of knowledge or someone who will give sincere counsel.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"3275","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:3275","g":"Sahih","n":null,"s":"The Prophet ﷺ confirmed that reciting Ayat al-Kursi before sleep keeps a devil away until morning.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6407","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6407","g":"Sahih","n":"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari","s":"The Prophet ﷺ said that the one who remembers his Lord and the one who does not are like the living and the dead.","l":"en"},{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5376","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5376","g":"Sahih","n":"'Umar ibn Abi Salamah","s":"‘Umar ibn Abi Salamah, who grew up in the care of the Prophet ﷺ, recalled being told as a boy to mention Allah’s name, eat with his right hand, and eat from what was in front of him.","l":"en"}],"duas":[{"t":"Before you sleep","m":null,"o":"Reciting Ayat al-Kursi before sleeping is reported in Sahih al-Bukhari 3275.","q":[2,255,255],"ar":null,"tr":null,"src":null},{"t":"When worry, weakness or debt is weighing on you","m":"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, from the burden of debt and from being overpowered by others.","o":"Reported in Sahih al-Bukhari 6363 as a supplication the Prophet ﷺ used to say. No number of repetitions is reported with it.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْهَمِّ وَالْحَزَنِ، وَالْعَجْزِ وَالْكَسَلِ، وَالْبُخْلِ وَالْجُبْنِ، وَضَلَعِ الدَّيْنِ وَغَلَبَةِ الرِّجَالِ","tr":"Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina l-hammi wa l-hazan, wa l-'ajzi wa l-kasal, wa l-bukhli wa l-jubn, wa dala'i d-dayni wa ghalabati r-rijal","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6363","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6363","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"For good in this life and the next","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[2,201,201],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana atina fi d-dunya hasanatan wa fi l-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhaba n-nar","src":null},{"t":"When you feel trapped and out of options","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[21,87,87],"ar":null,"tr":"La ilaha illa anta, subhanaka inni kuntu mina z-zalimin","src":null},{"t":"When more has been asked of you than you can carry","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[2,286,286],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana la tuhammilna ma la taqata lana bih, wa'fu 'anna waghfir lana warhamna","src":null},{"t":"Breaking your fast","m":"The thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, if Allah wills.","o":"Reported as said by him ﷺ on breaking his fast.","q":null,"ar":"ذَهَبَ الظَّمَأُ، وَابْتَلَّتِ الْعُرُوقُ، وَثَبَتَ الْأَجْرُ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ","tr":"Dhahaba z-zama'u, wa btallati l-'uruq, wa thabata l-ajru in sha'a Allah","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"2357","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2357","g":"Hasan (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"On Laylat al-Qadr","m":"O Allah, You are the One who pardons, and You love to pardon, so pardon me.","o":"Reported as taught by him ﷺ to ‘A’ishah, who asked what to say if she came upon Laylat al-Qadr.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّكَ عَفُوٌّ تُحِبُّ الْعَفْوَ فَاعْفُ عَنِّي","tr":"Allahumma innaka 'Afuwwun tuhibbu l-'afwa fa'fu 'anni","src":{"c":"Sunan Ibn Majah","r":"3850","u":"https://sunnah.com/ibnmajah:3850","g":"Sahih (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"Opening your eyes","m":"Praise be to Allah, who gave us life after having taken it from us, and to Him is the rising.","o":"Reported as said on waking.","q":null,"ar":"الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي أَحْيَانَا بَعْدَ مَا أَمَاتَنَا وَإِلَيْهِ النُّشُورُ","tr":"Al-hamdu lillahi lladhi ahyana ba'da ma amatana wa ilayhi n-nushur","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"7394","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:7394","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Waking up well","m":"Praise be to Allah, who kept my body sound, and returned my soul to me, and permitted me to remember Him.","o":"Reported as said on waking.","q":null,"ar":"الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي عَافَانِي فِي جَسَدِي وَرَدَّ عَلَيَّ رُوحِي وَأَذِنَ لِي بِذِكْرِهِ","tr":"Al-hamdu lillahi lladhi 'afani fi jasadi wa radda 'alayya ruhi wa adhina li bi dhikrih","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"3401","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:3401","g":"Sahih (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"On finishing the prayer","m":"O Allah, You are Peace and from You comes peace. Blessed are You, Possessor of Majesty and Honour.","o":"Reported as said by him ﷺ on finishing the prayer, after asking Allah’s forgiveness three times.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ السَّلاَمُ وَمِنْكَ السَّلاَمُ، تَبَارَكْتَ ذَا الْجَلاَلِ وَالإِكْرَامِ","tr":"Allahumma anta s-salamu wa minka s-salam, tabarakta dha l-jalali wa l-ikram","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"591","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:591","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"After the call to prayer","m":"O Allah, Lord of this complete call and of the prayer about to be established, grant Muhammad al-Wasilah and the place of honour, and raise him to the praised station You have promised him.","o":"Reported as said on hearing the call to prayer.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ رَبَّ هَذِهِ الدَّعْوَةِ التَّامَّةِ وَالصَّلاَةِ الْقَائِمَةِ، آتِ مُحَمَّدًا الْوَسِيلَةَ وَالْفَضِيلَةَ، وَابْعَثْهُ مَقَامًا مَحْمُودًا الَّذِي وَعَدْتَهُ","tr":"Allahumma Rabba hadhihi d-da'wati t-tammah, wa s-salati l-qa'imah, ati Muhammadan al-wasilata wa l-fadilah, wab'ath-hu maqaman mahmudan alladhi wa'adtah","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"614","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:614","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Finishing your wudu","m":"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone. He has no partner. And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.","o":"Reported as said on completing ablution.","q":null,"ar":"أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ","tr":"Ash-hadu an la ilaha illa Allahu wahdahu la sharika lah, wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"234b","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:234b","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"When you cannot manage on your own","m":"O Allah, it is Your mercy I hope for. Do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye. Put right all of my affairs. There is no god but You.","o":"Reported as said at a time of distress.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ رَحْمَتَكَ أَرْجُو فَلَا تَكِلْنِي إِلَى نَفْسِي طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ، وَأَصْلِحْ لِي شَأْنِي كُلَّهُ، لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ","tr":"Allahumma rahmataka arju fa la takilni ila nafsi tarfata 'ayn, wa aslih li sha'ni kullah, la ilaha illa ant","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"5090","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:5090","g":"Hasan in chain (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"When your temper rises","m":"I seek refuge in Allah from the devil, the outcast.","o":"Reported as what to say when anger takes hold.","q":null,"ar":"أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ","tr":"A'udhu billahi mina sh-shaytani r-rajim","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6115","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6115","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Asking to be grateful","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[27,19,19],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbi awzi'ni an ashkura ni'mataka llati an'amta 'alayya wa 'ala walidayya wa an a'mala salihan tardah, wa adkhilni bi-rahmatika fi 'ibadika s-salihin","src":null},{"t":"Counting the day's mercies","m":"Praise be to Allah, who fed us and gave us drink, and was enough for us, and gave us shelter. How many are there with no one to suffice them and nowhere to shelter.","o":"Reported as said on lying down to sleep.","q":null,"ar":"الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي أَطْعَمَنَا وَسَقَانَا، وَكَفَانَا، وَآوَانَا، فَكَمْ مِمَّنْ لَا كَافِيَ لَهُ وَلَا مُؤْوِيَ","tr":"Al-hamdu lillahi lladhi at'amana wa saqana, wa kafana, wa awana, fakam mimman la kafiya lahu wa la mu'wi","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2715","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2715","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"When you turn back to Allah and ask to be forgiven","m":"O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant. I keep to Your covenant and Your promise as far as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the harm of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favour upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You.","o":"Reported in Sahih al-Bukhari 6306, where the Prophet ﷺ taught it as the finest way of asking Allah for forgiveness.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ رَبِّي لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ، خَلَقْتَنِي وَأَنَا عَبْدُكَ، وَأَنَا عَلَى عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ، أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا صَنَعْتُ، أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِنِعْمَتِكَ عَلَيَّ، وَأَبُوءُ لَكَ بِذَنْبِي فَاغْفِرْ لِي، فَإِنَّهُ لَا يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ","tr":"Allahumma anta Rabbi, la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduk, wa ana 'ala 'ahdika wa wa'dika ma stata't. A'udhu bika min sharri ma sana't. Abu'u laka bi ni'matika 'alayya, wa abu'u laka bi dhanbi faghfir li, fa innahu la yaghfiru dh-dhunuba illa ant","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6306","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6306","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"When you have wronged yourself and want to return","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[7,23,23],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana zalamna anfusana wa in lam taghfir lana wa tarhamna lanakunanna mina l-khasirin","src":null},{"t":"Before something difficult you have to face","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[20,25,28],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbi shrah li sadri, wa yassir li amri, wahlul 'uqdatan min lisani, yafqahu qawli","src":null},{"t":"When something is pressing on you","m":"There is no god but Allah, the Great, the Forbearing. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of the Noble Throne.","o":"Reported as said at a time of distress.","q":null,"ar":"لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ الْعَظِيمُ الْحَلِيمُ، لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ، لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَرَبُّ الْأَرْضِ وَرَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيمِ","tr":"La ilaha illa Allahu l-'Azimu l-Halim, la ilaha illa Allahu Rabbu l-'arshi l-'azim, la ilaha illa Allahu Rabbu s-samawati wa Rabbu l-ardi wa Rabbu l-'arshi l-karim","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2730a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2730a","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"A few words to hold on to","m":"Allah, Allah is my Lord. I associate nothing with Him.","o":"Reported as said at a time of distress.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُ اللَّهُ رَبِّي لَا أُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا","tr":"Allahu Allahu Rabbi la ushriku bihi shay'a","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"1525","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:1525","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"When something has already gone wrong","m":"Allah decreed it, and He did what He willed.","o":"Reported as what to say when something has gone wrong, in place of \"if only\".","q":null,"ar":"قَدَّرَ اللَّهُ وَمَا شَاءَ فَعَلَ","tr":"Qaddara Allahu wa ma sha'a fa'al","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2664","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2664","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"When you are afraid, or outmatched","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[3,173,173],"ar":null,"tr":"Hasbunallahu wa ni'ma l-wakil","src":null},{"t":"When an affliction has gone on a long time","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[21,83,83],"ar":null,"tr":"Anni massaniya d-durru wa anta arhamu r-rahimin","src":null},{"t":"Asking for someone to be made well","m":"I ask Allah the Great, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to make you well.","o":"Reported as said when visiting someone who is unwell.","q":null,"ar":"أَسْأَلُ اللَّهَ الْعَظِيمَ، رَبَّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ، أَنْ يَشْفِيَكَ","tr":"As'alu Allaha l-'Azim, Rabba l-'arshi l-'azim, an yashfiyak","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"3106","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:3106","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"When something in your body hurts","m":"I seek refuge in Allah and in His power from the harm of what I feel and what I fear.","o":"Reported as said with your hand on the place that hurts, after saying \"In the name of Allah\" three times.","q":null,"ar":"أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ وَقُدْرَتِهِ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا أَجِدُ وَأُحَاذِرُ","tr":"A'udhu billahi wa qudratihi min sharri ma ajidu wa uhadhir","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2202","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2202","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"What to say to someone who is ill","m":"No harm. A cleansing, if Allah wills.","o":"Reported as said when visiting someone who is unwell.","q":null,"ar":"لَا بَأْسَ، طَهُورٌ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ","tr":"La ba'sa, tahurun in sha'a Allah","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"5656","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:5656","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"For your parents, living or passed","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[17,24,24],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbi rhamhuma kama rabbayani saghira","src":null},{"t":"When a loss or a calamity strikes","m":"O Allah, reward me in my affliction, and give me something better than it in its place.","o":"Reported in Sahih Muslim 918a as said when a calamity strikes, alongside the words the Qur’an teaches at 2:156.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ أْجُرْنِي فِي مُصِيبَتِي، وَأَخْلِفْ لِي خَيْرًا مِنْهَا","tr":"Allahumma'jurni fi musibati, wakhluf li khayran minha","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"918a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:918a","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"For those who have gone before us","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[59,10,10],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana ghfir lana wa li-ikhwanina lladhina sabaquna bi-l-iman, wa la taj'al fi qulubina ghillan li-lladhina amanu, Rabbana innaka Ra'ufun Rahim","src":null},{"t":"When you are afraid of people","m":"O Allah, we place You before them, and we seek refuge in You from their evil.","o":"Reported as said when he ﷺ feared a group of people.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّا نَجْعَلُكَ فِي نُحُورِهِمْ، وَنَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شُرُورِهِمْ","tr":"Allahumma inna naj'aluka fi nuhurihim, wa na'udhu bika min shururihim","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"1537","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:1537","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"The one he ﷺ said most often","m":"My Lord, forgive me and accept my turning back to You. You are the Ever-Relenting, the Forgiving.","o":"Reported as said by him ﷺ within a single sitting.","q":null,"ar":"رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَتُبْ عَلَيَّ إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الْغَفُورُ","tr":"Rabbi ghfir li wa tub 'alayya innaka anta t-Tawwabu l-Ghafur","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"3434","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:3434","g":"Sahih (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"Asking to be forgiven","m":"I ask forgiveness of Allah the Great, besides whom there is no god, the Living, the Sustainer, and I turn to Him.","o":"May be said at any time. The source names no particular occasion.","q":null,"ar":"أَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ الْعَظِيمَ الَّذِي لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ وَأَتُوبُ إِلَيْهِ","tr":"Astaghfiru Allaha l-'Azima lladhi la ilaha illa huwa l-Hayyu l-Qayyumu wa atubu ilayh","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"3577","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:3577","g":"Hasan (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"When doubt unsettles your heart","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[3,8,8],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana la tuzigh qulubana ba'da idh hadaytana wa hab lana min ladunka rahmah, innaka anta l-Wahhab","src":null},{"t":"For a righteous spouse and children","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[25,74,74],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbana hab lana min azwajina wa dhurriyyatina qurrata a'yunin waj'alna lil-muttaqina imama","src":null},{"t":"At the start of a marriage","m":"O Allah, I ask You for the good in her, and for the good of what You have made her inclined towards, and I seek refuge in You from the harm in her, and from the harm of what You have made her inclined towards.","o":"Reported as said at the start of a marriage.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ خَيْرَهَا، وَخَيْرَ مَا جَبَلْتَهَا عَلَيْهِ، وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّهَا، وَشَرِّ مَا جَبَلْتَهَا عَلَيْهِ","tr":"Allahumma inni as'aluka khayraha, wa khayra ma jabaltaha 'alayh, wa a'udhu bika min sharriha, wa sharri ma jabaltaha 'alayh","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"2160","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2160","g":"Hasan (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"What to say at a wedding","m":"May Allah bless you, and send blessings upon you, and bring you together in what is good.","o":"Reported as said to someone who has just married.","q":null,"ar":"بَارَكَ اللَّهُ لَكَ، وَبَارَكَ عَلَيْكَ، وَجَمَعَ بَيْنَكُمَا فِي خَيْرٍ","tr":"Baraka Allahu lak, wa baraka 'alayk, wa jama'a baynakuma fi khayr","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"2130","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2130","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"On getting up from a gathering","m":"Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I ask Your forgiveness and I turn to You.","o":"Reported as said on rising from a gathering.","q":null,"ar":"سُبْحَانَكَ اللَّهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ، أَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَأَتُوبُ إِلَيْكَ","tr":"Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdik, ash-hadu an la ilaha illa ant, astaghfiruka wa atubu ilayk","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"4859","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:4859","g":"Hasan Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"Placing a child in Allah's keeping","m":"I place you both in the keeping of the perfect words of Allah, from every devil and every crawling thing, and from every eye that harms.","o":"Reported as said by him ﷺ over al-Hasan and al-Husayn.","q":null,"ar":"أُعِيذُكُمَا بِكَلِمَاتِ اللَّهِ التَّامَّةِ، مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْطَانٍ وَهَامَّةٍ، وَمِنْ كُلِّ عَيْنٍ لَامَّةٍ","tr":"U'idhukuma bi kalimati Allahi t-tammah, min kulli shaytanin wa hammah, wa min kulli 'aynin lammah","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"2060","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:2060","g":"Sahih (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"Asking Allah for a child","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[3,38,38],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbi hab li min ladunka dhurriyyatan tayyibah, innaka sami'u d-du'a'","src":null},{"t":"Before studying, and whenever you seek knowledge","m":null,"o":"The Qur’an records this supplication. No source sets a time or a number of repetitions for it, so it may be said whenever you wish.","q":[20,114,114],"ar":null,"tr":"Rabbi zidni 'ilma","src":null},{"t":"When a debt will not settle","m":"O Allah, let what You have made lawful be enough for me instead of what You have forbidden, and by Your bounty make me need no one but You.","o":"Reported as taught for a debt that will not settle.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ اكْفِنِي بِحَلَالِكَ عَنْ حَرَامِكَ، وَأَغْنِنِي بِفَضْلِكَ عَمَّنْ سِوَاكَ","tr":"Allahumma kfini bi halalika 'an haramik, wa aghnini bi fadlika 'amman siwak","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"3563","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:3563","g":"Hasan (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"When you have paid someone back","m":"May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth. The repayment of a loan is thanks and the returning of it.","o":"Reported as said to someone who lent to you, once the loan is returned.","q":null,"ar":"بَارَكَ اللَّهُ لَكَ فِي أَهْلِكَ وَمَالِكَ، إِنَّمَا جَزَاءُ السَّلَفِ الْحَمْدُ وَالْأَدَاءُ","tr":"Baraka Allahu laka fi ahlika wa malik, innama jaza'u s-salafi l-hamdu wa l-ada'","src":{"c":"Sunan an-Nasa'i","r":"4683","u":"https://sunnah.com/nasai:4683","g":"Hasan (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"When you cannot decide","m":"O Allah, I ask You to choose for me by Your knowledge, and I ask You for the power to act by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You are able and I am not, and You know and I do not, and You are the Knower of all that is hidden. O Allah, if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion, my living and the outcome of my affairs, then decree it for me and make it easy for me, and then bless me in it. And if You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my living and the outcome of my affairs, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and decree for me what is good wherever it is, and then make me content with it.","o":"Reported as taught for any matter you are deciding, after praying two units of prayer outside the obligatory ones. Name the matter where the words say \"this matter\".","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْتَخِيرُكَ بِعِلْمِكَ، وَأَسْتَقْدِرُكَ بِقُدْرَتِكَ، وَأَسْأَلُكَ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ الْعَظِيمِ، فَإِنَّكَ تَقْدِرُ وَلَا أَقْدِرُ، وَتَعْلَمُ وَلَا أَعْلَمُ، وَأَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّ هَذَا الْأَمْرَ خَيْرٌ لِي فِي دِينِي وَمَعَاشِي وَعَاقِبَةِ أَمْرِي فَاقْدُرْهُ لِي وَيَسِّرْهُ لِي ثُمَّ بَارِكْ لِي فِيهِ، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّ هَذَا الْأَمْرَ شَرٌّ لِي فِي دِينِي وَمَعَاشِي وَعَاقِبَةِ أَمْرِي فَاصْرِفْهُ عَنِّي وَاصْرِفْنِي عَنْهُ، وَاقْدُرْ لِي الْخَيْرَ حَيْثُ كَانَ ثُمَّ أَرْضِنِي بِهِ","tr":"Allahumma inni astakhiruka bi 'ilmik, wa astaqdiruka bi qudratik, wa as'aluka min fadlika l-'azim, fa innaka taqdiru wa la aqdir, wa ta'lamu wa la a'lam, wa anta 'allamu l-ghuyub. Allahumma in kunta ta'lamu anna hadha l-amra khayrun li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa 'aqibati amri faqdurhu li wa yassirhu li thumma barik li fih. Wa in kunta ta'lamu anna hadha l-amra sharrun li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa 'aqibati amri fasrifhu 'anni wasrifni 'anh, waqdur li l-khayra haythu kana thumma ardini bih","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"1166","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1166","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Lying down for the night","m":"In Your name, my Lord, I lay down my side, and by You I raise it again. If You take my soul, have mercy on it; and if You send it back, then guard it as You guard Your righteous servants.","o":"Reported as said on lying down to sleep.","q":null,"ar":"بِاسْمِكَ رَبِّي وَضَعْتُ جَنْبِي، وَبِكَ أَرْفَعُهُ، فَإِنْ أَمْسَكْتَ نَفْسِي فَارْحَمْهَا، وَإِنْ أَرْسَلْتَهَا فَاحْفَظْهَا بِمَا تَحْفَظُ بِهِ عِبَادَكَ الصَّالِحِينَ","tr":"Bismika Rabbi wada'tu janbi, wa bika arfa'uh, fa in amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa in arsaltaha fahfazha bima tahfazu bihi 'ibadaka s-salihin","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6320","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6320","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Two lines before sleep","m":"In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live.","o":"Reported as said on lying down to sleep.","q":null,"ar":"بِاسْمِكَ اللَّهُمَّ أَمُوتُ وَأَحْيَا","tr":"Bismika Allahumma amutu wa ahya","src":{"c":"Sahih al-Bukhari","r":"6324","u":"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:6324","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Opening the day","m":"O Allah, by You we enter the morning and by You we enter the evening. By You we live and by You we die, and to You is the rising.","o":"Reported as said in the morning and again in the evening.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ بِكَ أَصْبَحْنَا، وَبِكَ أَمْسَيْنَا، وَبِكَ نَحْيَا، وَبِكَ نَمُوتُ، وَإِلَيْكَ النُّشُورُ","tr":"Allahumma bika asbahna, wa bika amsayna, wa bika nahya, wa bika namut, wa ilayka n-nushur","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"5068","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:5068","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"Asking to be kept safe on every side","m":"O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the next. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and for well-being in my religion, my worldly life, my family and my wealth. O Allah, cover what I would not have seen and settle what frightens me. O Allah, guard me from in front of me and behind me, from my right and my left and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being taken from beneath me.","o":"Reported as said in the morning and again in the evening.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ الْعَافِيَةَ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ الْعَفْوَ وَالْعَافِيَةَ فِي دِينِي وَدُنْيَايَ وَأَهْلِي وَمَالِي، اللَّهُمَّ اسْتُرْ عَوْرَاتِي وَآمِنْ رَوْعَاتِي، اللَّهُمَّ احْفَظْنِي مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيَّ وَمِنْ خَلْفِي وَعَنْ يَمِينِي وَعَنْ شِمَالِي وَمِنْ فَوْقِي، وَأَعُوذُ بِعَظَمَتِكَ أَنْ أُغْتَالَ مِنْ تَحْتِي","tr":"Allahumma inni as'aluka l-'afiyata fi d-dunya wa l-akhirah, Allahumma inni as'aluka l-'afwa wa l-'afiyata fi dini wa dunyaya wa ahli wa mali, Allahumma stur 'awrati wa amin raw'ati, Allahumma hfazni min bayni yadayya wa min khalfi wa 'an yamini wa 'an shimali wa min fawqi, wa a'udhu bi 'azamatika an ughtala min tahti","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"5074","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:5074","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"Going out of the door","m":"In the name of Allah. I have placed my trust in Allah. There is no strength and no power except by Allah.","o":"Reported as said on leaving the house.","q":null,"ar":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ، تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللَّهِ، وَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِاللَّهِ","tr":"Bismillah, tawakkaltu 'ala Allah, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"5095","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:5095","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"Setting out on a journey","m":"Glory be to the One who has placed this at our service, when we could never have mastered it ourselves, and to our Lord we will surely return. O Allah, on this journey of ours we ask You for righteousness and mindfulness of You, and for deeds that please You. O Allah, make this journey easy for us and shorten its distance for us. O Allah, You are the Companion on the journey and the One who looks after the family left behind. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, from a distressing sight, and from an unhappy return to my wealth and my family.","o":"Reported as said by him ﷺ on mounting to set out on a journey, after saying Allahu akbar three times. On returning he said the same words, and added: we return, repenting, worshipping and praising our Lord.","q":null,"ar":"سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي سَخَّرَ لَنَا هَذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهُ مُقْرِنِينَ، وَإِنَّا إِلَى رَبِّنَا لَمُنْقَلِبُونَ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّا نَسْأَلُكَ فِي سَفَرِنَا هَذَا الْبِرَّ وَالتَّقْوَى، وَمِنَ الْعَمَلِ مَا تَرْضَى، اللَّهُمَّ هَوِّنْ عَلَيْنَا سَفَرَنَا هَذَا، وَاطْوِ عَنَّا بُعْدَهُ، اللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ الصَّاحِبُ فِي السَّفَرِ، وَالْخَلِيفَةُ فِي الأَهْلِ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ وَعْثَاءِ السَّفَرِ، وَكَآبَةِ الْمَنْظَرِ، وَسُوءِ الْمُنْقَلَبِ فِي الْمَالِ وَالأَهْلِ","tr":"Subhana lladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin, wa inna ila Rabbina la-munqalibun. Allahumma inna nas'aluka fi safarina hadha l-birra wa t-taqwa, wa mina l-'amali ma tarda. Allahumma hawwin 'alayna safarana hadha, watwi 'anna bu'dah. Allahumma anta s-sahibu fi s-safar, wa l-khalifatu fi l-ahl. Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min wa'tha'i s-safar, wa ka'abati l-manzar, wa su'i l-munqalabi fi l-mali wa l-ahl","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"1342","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:1342","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Stopping somewhere new","m":"I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the harm of what He has created.","o":"Reported as said on stopping or staying somewhere.","q":null,"ar":"أَعُوذُ بِكَلِمَاتِ اللَّهِ التَّامَّاتِ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ","tr":"A'udhu bi kalimati Allahi t-tammati min sharri ma khalaq","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2708b","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2708b","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"Seeing somebody off","m":"I place in Allah's keeping your religion, what has been entrusted to you, and the ends of your deeds.","o":"Reported as said to somebody who is setting out.","q":null,"ar":"أَسْتَوْدِعُ اللَّهَ دِينَكَ وَأَمَانَتَكَ، وَخَوَاتِيمَ عَمَلِكَ","tr":"Astawdi'u Allaha dinaka wa amanatak, wa khawatima 'amalik","src":{"c":"Sunan Abi Dawud","r":"2600","u":"https://sunnah.com/abudawud:2600","g":"Sahih (per al-Albani)"}},{"t":"Entering the mosque","m":"O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy.","o":"Reported as taught for entering the mosque. The same narration teaches asking Allah for His bounty on leaving it.","q":null,"ar":"اللَّهُمَّ افْتَحْ لِي أَبْوَابَ رَحْمَتِكَ","tr":"Allahumma ftah li abwaba rahmatik","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"713a","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:713a","g":"Sahih"}},{"t":"After you have eaten","m":"Praise be to Allah, who fed me this and provided it for me, with no strength or power of my own.","o":"Reported as said after eating.","q":null,"ar":"الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي أَطْعَمَنِي هَذَا وَرَزَقَنِيهِ مِنْ غَيْرِ حَوْلٍ مِنِّي وَلَا قُوَّةٍ","tr":"Al-hamdu lillahi lladhi at'amani hadha wa razaqanih min ghayri hawlin minni wa la quwwah","src":{"c":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi","r":"3458","u":"https://sunnah.com/tirmidhi:3458","g":"Hasan (per Darussalam)"}},{"t":"A hundred times in a day","m":"Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Him.","o":"Reported as said in the course of a day.","q":null,"ar":"سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ وَبِحَمْدِهِ","tr":"Subhana Allahi wa bihamdih","src":{"c":"Sahih Muslim","r":"2691","u":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:2691","g":"Sahih"}}],"medical":"Alongside any dua or remembrance, please seek qualified medical care.","counts":{"topics":86,"quran":315,"narrations":69}};
